window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: Sefira","paragraphs":["The three men bowed once more before silently turning around. Their footsteps gradually faded into the distance until the enormous hall became silent once again.","Only Sefira remained. She quietly rested her cheek against one hand. For reasons she couldn’t understand.","Her thoughts once again drifted toward Noah Eldritch.","She unconsciously pressed her lips into a thin line. \"...Why am I thinking about him so often?\"","She couldn’t understand it. \"He was merely a frivolous young man. A shameless flirt. Just like countless other men. He even flirted with me. There was nothing special about that.\"","She slowly closed her eyes.","\"But... When I disguised myself. I wasn’t beautiful.\"","\"I deliberately appeared plain. An average, nerdy girl that no man would notice.\"","\"No one approached me. No one even looked twice.\"","She slowly opened her eyes again.","\"So...why did he? He even call me cute so many times.\"","That single question continued lingering inside her mind. The more she thought about it...","The stranger it seemed.","She quietly recalled the past several weeks.","\"...Now that I think about it...Other than me, he only ever flirt with Arisha and Lyria.\"","Her fingers lightly tapped against the armrest of the throne.","A displeased expression appeared on her face when she thought of him flirting with Arisha and Lyria.","Though his behavior hadn’t resembled that of a smooth flirt at all. Most of his pickup lines had been embarrassingly cheesy and cringe.","Some had even been downright ridiculous. None of them had sounded like the words of a man who truly knew how to win a woman’s heart.","She rubbed her chin thoughtfully.","\"...Perhaps he wasn’t serious.\"","Her voice was barely above a whisper.","\"Perhaps he was only teasing me.\"","Then another memory surfaced. She remembered the awkward smile on Noah’s face after she had questioned him.","He had scratched the back of his head and admitted that he had only been joking.","\"...Or...\"","Her brows knitted together.","\"...Was he actually trying to make someone fall for him... perhaps even me?\"","She immediately shook her head.","\"No... that doesn’t make any sense.\"","Yet another memory rose to the surface before she could dismiss it.","She remembered the sincerity in his glacier-blue eyes whenever he had called her cute and adorable.","There had been no hesitation.","He had genuinely seemed honest each time he call her that.","\"...Was he truly serious?\"","The question escaped her lips before she realized it. Her hand, which had been resting on the throne’s armrest, unconsciously tightened into a fist.","Crack.","Thin fractures spread across the ancient stone beneath her fingers.","She didn’t even notice. A faint blush slowly crept across her porcelain-white cheeks.","It was so subtle that almost no one would have noticed it.","’H-He didn’t actually... love me... right?’","Her flame like eyes widened slightly.","’No... What am I thinking...?’","She quickly shook her head, as though trying to drive the absurd thought from her mind.","’Impossible. Sefira... what’s wrong with you?’","’He was merely teasing you. Besides... I wasn’t even using my real appearance.’","She slowly leaned back against the throne.","Yet no matter how many times she tried to dismiss the thought...The image of Noah Eldritch refused to leave her mind.","She remembered the very first time she had met him.","It had been near the academy washroom. He had been cleaning the entire place as punishment after getting into a fight with another student. While he was getting out of the washroom she met him.","At the time she acted like young normal woman who felt afraid after hearing his name.","Then another memory surfaced.","She remembered his duel against Edward.","After the fight, while talking with Damien, he called her cute for first time. Then he had suddenly turned toward her with that familiar carefree smile.","Then, before leaving, he had said, ’I beat the hell out of Edward. If he ever comes back to you... just tell me.’","At the time, she had dismissed those words as nothing more than another one of his ridiculous attempts at flirting.","Another scene flashed before her eyes.","She had been quietly drinking coffee at a café when Noah had unexpectedly walked over and sat across from her.","Without any hesitation, he had asked if they could become friends.","That alone had shocked her.","She had never expected someone to approach her so naturally while she was disguised as nothing more than an ordinary girl.","In the end she had even exchanged communication numbers with him while acting like a shy, nervous girl.","Then, as if that wasn’t surprising enough, he had casually invited her to spend the weekend together.","Her brows furrowed slightly.","’...Was he really asking me out on a date?’","She quietly wondered. Unfortunately, too many incidents had followed afterward. Neither of them had ever gotten the chance to go on date.","She slowly shook her head.","’...What are you even thinking?’","Her thoughts drifted to another memory. It had been the incident involving the weakest form of a Monarch that was summoned by demon name Marbas.","That battle had nearly claimed lives of every students who were involved.","She had secretly interfered by freezing Marbas’s mind for a brief moment.","Those few precious seconds had given Noah the opening he needed to land the killing blow.","Afterward, she had immediately discovered the hidden exit.","As they ran, she had even formed an invisible barrier between Noah and the incoming attack from that terrifying creature.","Unfortunately the attack had been far too powerful.","Because her strength had been heavily suppressed by the artifact she wore, the barrier hadn’t lasted long.","Yet before the attack could reach her. Noah had pulled her into his arms without hesitation.","He had shielded her with his own body. They both were thrown out. After that she left that place to check the surrounding and came back when she sense Morgana running in that direction.","During that incident, it had been the first time something within her heart had changed.","For the first time she had felt that perhaps his words about wanting to become close to her... about wanting to be good friends hadn’t been lies after all.","From that day onward she had gradually begun feeling closer to him.","No matter how much she tried to deny it. She let out a long, helpless sigh.","’...My mind is being thrown into chaos by a nineteen-year-old boy?’","The thought alone filled her with embarrassment.","Perhaps... It was because she had spent so much time living as an ordinary nineteen-year-old academy student.","For the first time in a very long while she had experienced what it felt like to live a normal life.","Perhaps... She had simply become too immersed in it.","She didn’t know. Slowly, she bit her lower lip while recalling everything that had happened between them.","After remaining silent for a long while, she quietly muttered,","\"...Should I recruit him into my organization after he graduates from the academy?\"","---","[A/N: Hope u guys r happy seeing Mary alive. I have uploaded her image in comment section.]"]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Good Friend","paragraphs":["The evening sun bathed the academy campus in a warm orange glow.","Long shadows stretched across the stone pathways as students wandered through the grounds in small groups, chatting excitedly about the events of the examination.","Noah walked slowly along one of those paths.","Earlier that day, he had finally been discharged from the academy infirmary.","Physically, most of his injuries had healed.","Mentally he still hadn’t recovered.","His footsteps were slow and heavy as he listened to the distant chatter around him.","While speaking with Instructor Morgana before leaving the infirmary, he had learned that the First Semester Examination had officially been canceled.","After the demon attack, the academy had decided it was too dangerous to continue.","There would be no retest.","Instead, the final rankings would be determined by the number of monsters each student had defeated before the incident, combined with the results of the VR Combat Unit Test.","Students who had participated in the battle against the demons would also receive additional merit points.","Because of his performance in the VR test and his contribution to defeating the demons, Noah would almost certainly finish within the academy’s top ten.","Under normal circumstances, that news would have made him genuinely happy.","Today he couldn’t bring himself to care.","The academy had also officially entered its summer vacation.","Students laughed together as they discussed where they planned to travel or how they intended to spend the break.","Their cheerful voices faded into meaningless background noise.","Despite another incident happened, students were not so much worried. After all only one student died. And it was not something that had occurred with them.","None of it reached Noah.","After walking aimlessly for several minutes, he stopped beneath a large maple tree whose leaves rustled gently in the evening breeze.","A simple wooden bench rested beneath its shade.","He quietly sat down. Leaning against the backrest, he lifted his gaze toward the orange sky.","His thoughts drifted back to everything that had happened over the past few days.","Mary’s smile. Her quiet voice. The moment she had pushed him away. The image of the sword piercing through her chest.","He slowly closed his eyes.","He had always known there would come a day when someone close to him might die. This world wasn’t peaceful.","It was filled with monsters, demons, and countless dangers.","Death was inevitable. He had understood that when he came to this world. At least he had believed he did. He had thought he would accept it more easily.","He had been wrong. It hurt far more than he had ever imagined.","A tired sigh escaped his lips.","He simply wanted someone beside him. Someone who would quietly listen. If he remained alone the thought of that incident would come back to him again and again.","For some reason one person came to mind.","Lyria.","She had visited him in the infirmary with the others the day after the incident.","Yesterday she had even returned alone to check on him.","So Noah took out his phone and called her. The call had barely connected when a soft, familiar voice reached his ears.","\"Noah.\"","Her gentle voice sounded almost like a soothing melody carried by the evening breeze. He instinctively lifted his head.","Standing only a few meters away was Lyria. Her long golden-blonde hair flowed freely behind her instead of being tied as usual.","She wore a simple white blouse beneath a light beige cardigan, paired with a modest blue skirt that swayed gently with each step.","The warm light of the setting sun gave her soft pink eyes an even gentler glow.","She smiled faintly as she approached him.","\"So you were here.\"","Noah managed a small smile.","\"I guess... you found me faster than I expected. I was just going to call you.\"","She let out a quiet laugh before sitting beside him on the bench. She sat close enough that their shoulders nearly touched.","For a brief moment, neither of them spoke. The silence between them wasn’t awkward.","It felt comfortable.","Lyria finally turned toward him.","\"I was on my way to infirmary, to meet you. And then saw you here.\"","Her voice carried unmistakable concern.","\"So you’ve finally been discharged.\"","She studied his face carefully.","\"Are you feeling alright?\"","Noah looked down at his hands resting on his lap.","\"...Yeah.\"","He paused before quietly correcting himself.","\"No... I don’t think I am.\"","His voice sounded tired.","\"I just...\"","He searched for the right words.","\"...wanted someone to t be with me.\"","Lyria’s expression softened. Without hesitation, she gently placed her hand over his.","Her touch was warm.","\"I know.\"","Her thumb softly brushed across the back of his hand.","\"You’re grieving because of Mary.\"","Noah remained silent.","Lyria continued quietly.","\"You two were close.\"","A small smile appeared on her face as she recalled something.","\"To be honest... I don’t think I ever saw Mary talk to anyone as much as she talked to you.\"","Noah lowered his gaze.","\"...Yeah.\"","His voice had become almost a whisper.","\"I really miss her.\"","He swallowed slowly.","\"And...\"","His fingers unconsciously tightened.","\"I’m hurting even more because...she died protecting me.\"","His words barely escaped his lips.","Lyria’s heart ached.","This was the first time she had ever seen Noah like this.","The Noah she knew was always smiling.","Always teasing others.","Especially her and Arisha.","He somehow always found a way to embarrass her with one of his ridiculous compliments. Yet the young man sitting beside her now looked completely different.","His blue eyes had lost their usual brightness. His shoulders seemed heavier than ever before.","For Lyria who was from the holy region, the dukedom that was strictly religious. She was raised in a way to show kindness to other. And because of that she felt more worried for Noah.","Even his smile had disappeared.","She quietly watched him for a few moments before speaking again.","\"Noah...Mary made that decision herself.\"","Her voice remained soft and gentle.","\"She chose to protect you.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"Even if it meant sacrificing her own life.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"That only proves how much she cared about you.\"","Noah slowly shook his head.","\"I know.\"","His voice trembled slightly.","\"I understand that.\"","\"But...\"","He clenched his fists.","\"How could she throw away her own life just to save mine?\"","Lyria looked at him silently.","Then she asked one simple question.","\"...If your positions had been reversed...\"","She paused briefly.","\"...Wouldn’t you have done exactly the same for her?\"","Noah froze.","He didn’t answer immediately.","Instead he imagined Mary standing where he had been.","A sword aimed at her.","Would he have hesitated? Not even for a second.","He slowly nodded.","\"...I would have.\""]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: Family Visit","paragraphs":["His answer came without the slightest uncertainty.","To be honest ever since arriving in this world, Noah had often wondered whether returning to Earth was possible.","Perhaps... If he managed to reach the ending of the game. If he succeeded in preventing the world’s destruction.","Maybe then there would be a way home. Unfortunately he had no knowledge of what truly awaited him in the future.","Ironically, that uncertainty never frightened him as much as it probably should have. Maybe he had been more frightened and worried if he knew about the future.","He spent every day growing stronger.","He was training everyday.","Preparing for dangers he couldn’t even predict. But one thing had never changed. No matter how desperately he wished to survive.","He couldn’t bring himself to sacrifice the people he cared about.","He wasn’t a hero. He knew that much. He wasn’t someone who wanted to save everyone. But neither was he someone capable of abandoning those precious to him simply to preserve his own life.","If it had been anyone other than Mary, someone Noah wasn’t close to, he wouldn’t have felt this way. He always felt bad when innocent people died, but it was usually just a momentary sadness","He was sure about that.","\"...Noah.\"","Lyria called his name once more.","He slowly turned toward her.","\"Hm?\"","Before he could say anything else...","Lyria gently leaned forward.","Then, without a word. She wrapped both arms around him.","Pulling him into a soft, warm embrace.","Her hug wasn’t passionate. Nor was it impulsive.","It was quiet gentle and comforting. As though she simply wanted to tell him. He didn’t have to carry all of that pain alone.","Her hand gently patted his back in a slow, comforting rhythm.","Noah slowly closed his eyes. Without realizing it, he rested his face against the crook of her neck. A soft, sweet fragrance surrounded him.","It was warm and comforting.","The heaviness weighing down on his heart eased, even if only a little. He didn’t say anything. Neither did Lyria.","She simply continued holding him quietly, allowing him to grieve in silence.","The gentle breeze rustled the leaves above them while the last rays of the evening sun filtered through the branches.","The world around them seemed to fade away.","For a brief moment only the two of them remained. They stayed like that for quite a while.","---","Splash!","Cold water struck Noah’s face.","Tiny droplets slid down his cheeks before falling into the sink below. He slowly lifted his head and looked at his reflection in the mirror.","His blue eyes still appeared somewhat tired.","He exhaled softly.","\"...I feel a little better.\"","The conversation with Lyria had helped him more than he had expected.","His heart still hurt. Mary’s death still weighed heavily on his mind.","That pain wouldn’t disappear overnight.","Perhaps it never truly would.","Still he couldn’t allow himself to remain trapped in sorrow forever.","He stared silently at his reflection for another few moments.","\"I can’t keep dwelling on the past.\"","His voice was quiet but determined.","\"...Whatever happened... already happened. There isn’t any way to change it.\"","He lowered his gaze.","\"I have to move forward. I have to focus on what’s ahead.\"","After a brief silence, another thought crossed his mind.","\"...Summer vacation has already started.\"","A faint smile appeared on his lips.","\"And Brother Nathan told me to come home.\"","He reached for the towel hanging beside the sink and slowly dried his face before leaving the bathroom.","The dormitory room was unusually quiet. The evening sunlight streamed gently through the window, painting the wooden floor with warm golden light.","Curled comfortably on the bed was Nancy. The black cat lazily raised her head the moment Noah entered before letting out a quiet meow.","\"Meow~\"","A small smile naturally appeared on Noah’s face. He walked over and lay down on the bed with a tired sigh.","He tried to pull the cat toward him.","Understanding what he was trying to do, Nancy immediately climbed onto him without hesitation. She circled twice before curling up comfortably on his chest.","Noah gently stroked her soft black fur.","His fingers slowly ran through it while Nancy purred contentedly beneath his touch. The soothing vibration echoed against his chest. \"...You’re really spoiled now.\"","Nancy responded only by rubbing her head against his hand. As he absentmindedly continued petting her. A certain memory surfaced in his mind.","Lyria’s embrace.","Her warmth.","The gentle fragrance that had surrounded her.","Before he realized it a faint blush spread across his cheeks.","\"...Man...\"","He covered part of his face with one hand.","\"I didn’t think much about it back then but she really hugged me.\"","He let out an embarrassed sigh.","\"And I ended up acting like a complete child.\"","Remembering himself burying his face against her shoulder made him want to hide under the blanket forever.","\"...That’s seriously embarrassing.\"","He rubbed the back of his neck awkwardly.","\"Lyria is just... too kind.\"","He smiled helplessly.","\"I shouldn’t misunderstand her kindness.\"","For a brief moment after returning to his dormitory. The thought had crossed his mind.","’Could she possibly... like me?’","It had only lasted for an instant.","He immediately shook his head.","\"No.\"","\"...That’s impossible. Lyria has always been kind to everyone. She’s simply that kind of person.\"","He wasn’t foolish enough to mistake genuine compassion for romantic feelings.","At least he didn’t want to.","A small smile appeared on his face.","\"Still I should repay her someday. She really helped me when I needed someone.\"","His expression gradually became more complicated.","\"...Dammit.\"","He sighed while staring at the ceiling.","\"Then there’s my family...\"","He hadn’t visited home in quite some time. Nathan had already reminded him before the examination.","Now that summer vacation had begun...","There was no longer any excuse to postpone it.","\"...I guess I should go.\"","He gently scratched Nancy beneath her chin.","\"Maybe after a few days.\"","Nancy lazily purred in response, completely unconcerned about his troubles.","Noah smiled faintly.","After so many moths of being exiled. It was finally time to return home and see his family once again.","Then his thought went back to his conversation with Lyria. After hug they did talk more.","It was about her innate ability.","’Purification...’"]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: New Abilities","paragraphs":["The following morning.","The academy training grounds were far quieter than usual.","With summer vacation having officially begun, most of the students had already returned home. Only a handful remained behind, using the academy’s facilities to continue training.","The rhythmic sounds of clashing weapons and exploding spells echoed across the open field.","Noah sat alone on a wooden bench beneath the shade of a large tree, quietly watching the students spar and train.","He came to train this morning and now he was taking some rest.","After everything that had happened, after the battle against the demons, after Mary’s death.","He had finally decided it was time to properly examine the changes to his Status.","He hadn’t looked at it carefully since the examination.","Closing his eyes for a brief moment, he muttered inwardly,","’Status.’","A familiar translucent blue screen immediately materialized before him.","It floated silently in the air.","=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 327 [+87]","Speed: 330 [+83]","Stamina: 339 [+81]","Endurance: 321 [+86]","Charm: 631","Mana: 3123 [+570]","Core Rank: Awakened (High)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.2]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist], [Ice Blizzard]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Ability: [Adaptive Learning], [Heart of absolute Frost]","Active Ability:[Monarch’s Decree]","Bloodline: [Monarch of The Frost]","=================","Noah quietly studied every line.","His gaze lingered on his attributes.","\"...My stats increased again.\"","The increase was far greater than he had expected.","He folded his arms while thinking.","’Was it because of the System?Or because of the Moon Goddess?’","The mysterious encounter after the battle surfaced in his mind.","He still didn’t know whether it had truly happened or if it had merely been a dream.","After remaining silent for a while, another possibility crossed his mind.","’Or perhaps, did my growth speed increase because my Potential changed into Mythical?’","He couldn’t tell about his sudden growth..","There simply wasn’t enough information. Eventually, his attention shifted toward the newly awakened abilities.","His gaze stopped on Heart of Absolute Frost.","\"...This passive ability is incredible.\"","At first glance, it didn’t appear particularly impressive.","However the more he analyzed its description, the more terrifying it became.","First of all he had become immune to cold.","He could still feel low temperatures. But they no longer affected his body.","Whether it was freezing snow, a glacier or even supernatural ice.","His body could endure temperatures that would instantly kill an ordinary person.","He smiled faintly. \"If a spell capable of reaching absolute zero actually existed, it probably wouldn’t be able to freeze me.\"","Noah had read about such spells in many webnovels. But now they won’t affect him.","For someone who possessed the bloodline of the Frost Monarch such an ability was almost perfect.","He glanced toward the clear summer sky. Despite the intense heat of the morning sun.","His body felt pleasantly cool.","\"...This is surprisingly comfortable.\"","He chuckled softly.","\"I’ll never have to complain about summer again.\"","After a few more moments, his gaze shifted downward once more.","This time he focused on his active ability.","Monarch’s Decree.","Unlike Heart of the Absolute Frost, this ability wasn’t passive.","It required conscious activation. According to the information that came to him naturally. As if it existed there from the beginning.","It allowed him to release the oppressive aura of the Monarch.","Against opponents weaker than himself, that pressure could instill fear, suppress their movements, and even force simple commands upon them.","For example if he ordered someone to Freeze, their body would become temporarily immobilized.","The duration depended on the opponent’s mental strength and overall power.","The stronger the enemy, the weaker the effect would be.","\"...That’s absurdly useful.\"","He leaned back against the bench.","’I really want to test it...’","His blue eyes slowly swept across the training grounds.","Only a few students remained. Most of them were busy practicing with swords or casting spells.","\"...Who here is weaker than me?\"","He honestly had no idea.","At that moment a young man with short dark brown hair began walking toward the same bench Noah occupied.","The student wiped the sweat from his forehead with a towel hanging around his neck.","He appeared exhausted after training.","Noah had noticed him training several minutes earlier.","Judging from his movements and training, he was clearly weaker than Noah.","’...Perfect.Alright. Let’s give it a try on him. It’s not like my ability would harm him physically.’","Noah slowly exhaled.","Then he activated Monarch’s Decree.","The change happened instantly. An indescribable chill spread throughout his entire body.","It wasn’t ordinary cold.","It resembled the state he entered while performing the Second Petal of the Frozen Lotus Blade Art.","A state in which every emotion disappeared.","However there was one crucial difference.","When using the Second Petal Noah had to deliberately suppress every emotion himself.","He needed complete concentration.","Monarch’s Decree was different.","The emotions simply vanished without effort and without any resistance.","His grief over Mary’s death disappeared. His anxiety about returning home faded away.","His guilt, his anger and even his lingering sadness, everything became distant.","Only absolute calm remained.","Cold, emotionless indifferent was all inside him.","A pale glacier-blue light gradually filled his eyes. His pupils seemed to glow with an ethereal frost.","At that exact moment the approaching student instinctively looked toward Noah.","Their eyes met.","Thump!","The young man’s heartbeat suddenly accelerated.","Every instinct in his body screamed at him.","He felt danger.","An overwhelming pressure descended upon him without warning.","His breathing became shallow.","His legs instinctively wanted to retreat.","Yet they refused to obey.","Noah looked directly into his eyes. Then, in a calm, indifferent voice, he uttered a single word.","\"Freeze.\"","The moment those words left his mouth. The young man’s body completely stiffened.","He couldn’t move. He couldn’t even move a finger.","His pupils shrank. ’W-What’s happening...?’","Panic spread through his mind. His heart pounded violently inside his chest.","Thump.","Thump.","Thump.","Cold sweat rolled down his forehead. His breathing became uneven.","An indescribable fear slowly crept into every corner of his mind.","It wasn’t merely fear.","It felt as though an existence far above him had spoken. And his body had no choice but to obey.","Click.","Click.","Click.","Footsteps echoed across the training ground.","They grew closer with every approaching step the pressure became heavier.","The young man’s breathing turned increasingly ragged.","His entire body trembled uncontrollably. He wanted to look up. He wanted to run. He wanted to scream.","But none of his muscles responded. The footsteps finally reached him.","Then without stopping they calmly passed by.","Click.","Click.","Click.","The pressure disappeared. His frozen body suddenly regained control.","Thud!","His knees struck the ground. Both hands slammed against the dirt as he desperately caught himself.","\"Haah...!\"","\"Haah...!\"","He gasped for air as though he had nearly drowned. His entire body shook uncontrollably.","Sweat soaked his clothes.","Slowly he turned around. Only one figure remained in his sight.","A young man with snow-white hair calmly walked away from the wooden bench, his back facing him.","Without looking back even once Noah quietly left the training grounds.","---","Inside one of the academy’s spacious stone corridors, Noah walked at a leisurely pace while absentmindedly rubbing his forehead.","\"Hmm... just as I expected.\"","He let out a quiet sigh.","\"This ability really does put some pressure on my mind.\"","The headache was mild, little more than a dull ache behind his forehead but it was noticeable.","Fortunately, it wasn’t severe enough to affect his movements or concentration.","\"It’s manageable.\"","He lowered his hand and continued walking through the corridor.","As he walked, the image of the young student he had tested Monarch’s Decree on replayed in his mind.","\"The effect was far stronger than I expected.\"","A faint smile appeared on his lips.","\"He was completely terrified.\"","The memory of the student’s trembling body, cold sweat, and inability to move confirmed just how frightening the ability truly was.","Their very soul seemed to recognize the overwhelming presence standing before them.","\"A useful ability...\"","Noah muttered to himself.","\"If used properly, it could completely disrupt an enemy before the battle even began.\"","His thoughts soon drifted elsewhere.","\"Once I returned home...\"","A small smile appeared on his face.","\"...I could ask Father and Brother Nathan to put me through few rounds of training.\"","Noah actually looked forward to training with them. Both of them possessed far more experience than he did.","\"It’ll be worth it.\"","Just then, \"Noah!\"","A familiar voice called out from behind him.","Noah stopped walking and turned around.","He saw Damien approaching together with the rest of his usual group.","Leonard walked beside him with his carefree grin.","Kaelan followed quietly.","Lyria and Arisha were walking together while Emma trailed slightly behind them.","The six of them soon reached Noah.","Damien looked him over before speaking.","\"How are you feeling now? I heard from Lyria that you were discharged yesterday evening.\"","\"I’m doing much better.\"","A small smile appeared on Noah’s face.","\"The healers did an excellent job.\"","\"That’s good to hear.\"","Arisha smiled gently, relief evident in her emerald eyes.","\"We were all worried about you.\"","Leonard crossed his arms and laughed.","\"Honestly, he’s Noah. I knew he’d recover ridiculously fast.\"","\"You’re giving me too much credit.\"","Noah chuckled softly.","Even Emma, who usually never missed an opportunity to criticize him, cleared her throat awkwardly.","\"...I’m glad you’re alright.\"","She immediately looked away after saying it, clearly embarrassed.","Noah blinked in surprise.","That might have been the first genuinely kind thing she had ever said to him.","A faint smile formed on his face.","\"Thank you.\"","Emma simply folded her arms and muttered something under her breath.","The atmosphere around the group became much lighter.","Noah’s gaze eventually shifted toward Kaelan.","\"More importantly...How are you doing?\"","Kaelan nodded.","\"I’m fine. My injuries have mostly healed.\"","Noah hesitated for a moment before asking the question that had been lingering in his mind.","\"Did your family or the academy discover why those demons were trying to assassinate you?\"","Kaelan’s expression became serious.","He slowly shook his head.","\"No. Neither the academy nor my family has found anything yet. They’re still investigating. No one knows why the demons specifically targeted me.\"","A thoughtful silence followed.","\"I hope they find something soon.\"","\"So do I.\"","Kaelan nodded quietly.","The group continued walking together through the corridor.","The gentle morning breeze drifted in through the enormous open windows, carrying the refreshing scent of flowers from the academy gardens."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: On A Date?","paragraphs":["After walking together for a while, the group eventually reached a crossroads within the academy grounds.","Kaelan stopped first.","\"I’ll be leaving now,\" he said. \"Father already sent people to pick me up.\"","Leonard stretched lazily before grinning.","\"I should head home too.\"","Emma simply nodded.","\"I have to leave as well.\"","The three of them exchanged farewells before walking toward the academy’s main gate, disappearing into the steady stream of students who were leaving for the summer holidays.","Soon, only Noah, Damien, Lyria, and Arisha remained.","The four of them continued strolling through the academy campus.","It was still morning.","The gentle sunlight bathed the stone pathways in a warm golden glow, while a cool breeze rustled the leaves of the ancient trees lining the roads. Groups of students chatted cheerfully as they carried luggage toward the academy gates, eager to return home after the semester had ended.","Noah glanced sideways at Damien.","\"What about you?\"","Damien scratched the back of his head before letting out a long sigh.","\"I’ll have to stay here for another day or two. Master Morgana won’t let me leave until she give some training to me.\"","He sounded utterly defeated. \"It’s going to be nothing but training from morning until night. Only after that will she allow me to go home.\"","Noah nodded knowingly.","\"That’s understandable. She’s probably worried that you’ll neglect your training during the holidays.\"","Damien immediately frowned.","\"Hey! I’ve never neglected my training. You should know better than anyone that I enjoy training all day.\"","Noah chuckled.","\"Yes, yes. I’ve heard that speech enough times.\"","Damien rolled his eyes before laughing as well.","\"Anyway, I’d better get going. Master is probably waiting for me already.\"","\"Alright.\"","Noah raised a hand casually.","\"Tell your master I miss her.\"","Both Lyria and Arisha, who had been quietly listening beside them, instinctively turned toward Noah.","Their brows furrowed slightly. Normally, they would have assumed he was teasing someone again.","However there wasn’t even the slightest trace of mischief on Noah’s face this time.","His expression remained completely calm. That made it impossible to tell whether he had been joking... or whether he had genuinely meant it.","Damien simply laughed.","\"I’ll tell her.\"","He waved one last time.","\"See you all later.\"","\"Bye.\"","Lyria smiled warmly.","\"Take care.\"","Arisha nodded calmly.","Damien soon disappeared into another path leading toward the instructors’ residence.","Silence settled between the remaining three.","Noah turned toward the two girls.","\"So...You two aren’t leaving today?\"","Arisha shook her head.","\"No. We decided to stay here for a few more days.\"","She wore a simple black short-sleeved shirt beneath a light gray jacket, paired with dark trousers that allowed easy movement. Her long violet hair was tied into a practical ponytail.","Lyria smiled softly.","\"It’s almost one and a half months of vacation. We have plenty of time. There’s no reason to rush home.\"","Unlike Arisha’s practical attire, Lyria wore a flowing white blouse beneath a light blue cardigan with a knee-length cream-colored skirt. Her long golden-blonde hair flowed freely down her back, swaying gently with every breeze, while her gentle pink eyes carried their usual warmth.","\"Fair enough.\"","Noah nodded.","\"So what are your plans for these next couple of days?\"","Arisha answered immediately.","\"Nothing special. I’ll rest...and enjoy the cafeteria’s free food while I still can.\"","Noah laughed softly.","\"That’s actually not a bad plan.\"","Lyria hesitated for a brief moment before gathering her courage.","\"If you don’t mind...Would you like to visit the temple together?\"","There was a faint excitement in her gentle voice.","Noah looked at her before smiling.","Being around these two somehow made his heart feel calmer. The heaviness weighing on his chest had eased, if only slightly.","\"Sure. I was actually thinking about confessing something again. Maybe I’ll get lucky and have the same priestess as last time.\"","The moment those words left his mouth...","Lyria froze.","The memories from their previous visit of Noah to the temple immediately resurfaced.","She remembered every ridiculous confession Noah had made that day.","Her cheeks instantly turned pink.","\"H-Hey! I don’t think you need to use the confession booth this time!\"","Noah shrugged innocently.","\"Come on. I’ll feel better after confessing.\"","Arisha looked back and forth between the two of them.","Her sharp instincts immediately sensed something unusual. The way Lyria had reacted and Noah’s calm smile.","Something had definitely happened between them during their previous visit.","She narrowed her eyes slightly.","\"Noah...\"","He looked at her.","\"Hm?\"","\"Are you really feeling alright?\"","As she spoke, she gently placed her hand over his.","Noah blinked in surprise.","Her fingers felt soft against his skin, though he could also feel the faint calluses along her fingertips, a clear sign of the countless hours she had spent practicing archery.","He looked at her before giving her a gentle smile.","\"I’m fine now. Much better than before. So don’t worry.\"","Arisha studied his face for another second before suddenly speaking.","\"Then how about going on a date with me?\"","\"What?!\"","Lyria practically shouted.","Her pink eyes widened in disbelief. She looked far more shocked than Noah himself.","Noah simply stared at Arisha for a second before sighing. He could already tell she was joking.","Or perhaps she was simply trying to cheer him up in her own awkward way.","\"A date?\"","He scratched his cheek.","\"To be honest...I’m not really in the mood.\"","\"Tch.\"","Arisha clicked her tongue.","\"You just wasted a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.\"","\"H-Hey!\"","Lyria protested, her cheeks becoming even redder.","\"W-Why are you saying things like that?! Also why are you deciding those things by yourself?\"","Noah laughed.","\"Still...I wouldn’t mind going out somewhere. We’ve never actually explored Novaris City together.\"","Lyria immediately brightened.","\"I’d like that. It sounds fun.\"","Arisha folded her arms.","\"That’s just another way of saying ’date.’ You’re only changing the name to normal outing between friends.\"","Noah clicked his tongue.","\"Tch. Fine. Honestly it would’ve sounded less suspicious if Damien had come with us.\"","Arisha snorted.","\"Let him train. That guy’s a complete training fanatic.\"","\"That’s exactly why he’s the strongest student in our class.\"","\"So?\"","Arisha replied without the slightest concern.","Noah blinked.","He found her reaction surprisingly interesting. According to the character list he read. She was a female lead.","Arisha was meant to become Damien’s love interest.","Yet there wasn’t the slightest sign of admiration or romantic interest in her voice whenever Damien was mentioned.","If anything she treated him no differently than anyone else.","Noah silently wondered whether the future had already begun to change.","Eventually, he shook his head.","\"Well... I honestly don’t know what to say anymore. But I don’t want to fall behind Damien.\"","\"You won’t, you also train like him all day. I can’t understand how you two do that.\" Arisha said with amusement.","\"Arisha, you are not different. You read and study lot of things about magic for hours.\"","Arisha herself was hard working young woman. Yet calling another men training freak, that was definitely wrong."]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Whatever you say, dear","paragraphs":["Lyria then decided to changed the topic. She clapped her hands lightly before smiling.","\"Let’s stop standing around. We should get going.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Agreed. No point wasting the morning.\"","\"True, let’s go.\"","The three of them walked side by side toward the academy gates, their figures gradually disappearing beneath the warm summer sunlight as they headed toward Novaris City together.","---","The three of them walked side by side through the lively streets of Novaris City.","The morning had gradually given way to late morning. As they walked, Arisha suddenly glanced at Noah with an amused smile.","\"So How does it feel, Noah?\"","Noah looked at her in confusion.","\"Hm? About what?\"","Arisha folded her arms behind her head as she continued walking.","\"I meant How does it feel to spend time alone with two beautiful young ladies?\"","Noah immediately knew where the conversation was heading. He opened his mouth, intending to tell her to stop teasing him again.","However before he could answer, Lyria spoke from his other side.","\"You are doing it again?\"","She looked at Arisha with a helpless expression.","\"Please stop teasing him.\"","Unlike Arisha, Lyria became embarrassed far too easily.","Hearing conversations like these always made her cheeks warm.","Arisha simply shrugged innocently.","\"Alright. I’ll stop.\"","A small smile appeared on her lips before she changed the topic.","\"Where should we go first?\"","Noah answered almost immediately.","\"Food.\"","The two girls looked at him.","\"I didn’t eat breakfast this morning. And it’s almost noon already. If we eat something now, there won’t be any need to have lunch later.\"","\"That sounds reasonable.\" Lyria said.","Arisha nodded. \"I don’t mind.\"","Then she looked at Noah with a mischievous smile. \"Whatever you say, dear.\"","Lyria sighed the moment she heard that. \"She really isn’t going to stop...\"","Noah laughed softly.","\"Just let her. She enjoys teasing me. There’s no point trying to stop her.\"","Lyria could only smile helplessly.","\"...Well, if you say so.\"","The three of them continued walking until they found a cozy restaurant that specialized in burgers and pizzas.","The moment they stepped inside, the rich aroma of melted cheese, freshly baked bread, and grilled meat greeted them.","Several customers were already enjoying their meals while soft music played quietly in the background.","After finding an empty table beside a large window overlooking the busy street, they sat down.","The waiter soon arrived. Noah ordered a large burger and a pizza to share.","Lyria and Arisha ordered the same.","After handing back the menus, they quietly waited for their food.","Noah rested one arm on the table.","\"After this...How about we go shopping?\"","Lyria nodded.","\"I’d like that. It’s been quite a while since I bought any new clothes.\"","Arisha shrugged casually.","\"I don’t mind.\"","A brief silence followed.","Then Noah suddenly turned toward Arisha.","\"By the way... Can I ask you something?\"","She looked at him.","\"What is it?\"","Noah hesitated for a second before speaking.","\"I’ve always wondered...Why are you so casual around me? You joke with me all the time in weird way. I’ve never seen you talk like this with any other guy.\"","Arisha blinked.","She raised one hand and gently tapped her chin with her index finger. Her yellow eyes drifted toward the bustling street beyond the large glass window.","She genuinely seemed to be thinking about the answer.","Even Lyria became curious.","She quietly waited for Arisha’s reply.","After several moments, Arisha finally spoke.","\"...How should I explain it?\"","She looked back at Noah.","\"When I first saw you...I honestly thought you were really handsome.\"","Noah froze.","\"...Huh?\"","Even Lyria’s eyes widened in surprise. Neither of them had expected such a straightforward answer.","Noah knew Arisha well enough to understand one thing. She wasn’t the type of girl who became interested in someone simply because they were attractive.","Which made her answer even more unexpected.","Arisha continued calmly.","\"Then we talked while walking to meet the principal. I remember you calling me beautiful.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"I could clearly tell you were teasing me.\"","\"So...I decided to play along.\"","She shrugged.","\"And honestly...It was kind of fun.\"","Realization dawned on Noah.","\"So that’s why you kept teasing me afterward.\"","She nodded.","\"Exactly. You kept flirting with those unbelievably cheesy and cringe lines...\"","\"So I simply continued playing along.\"","Noah immediately protested.","\"Hey!\"","\"They weren’t cheesy or cringe.\"","\"And besides...I deliberately flirted badly. I didn’t want anyone to actually take those lines seriously. I made them... cringe on purpose.\"","Lyria slowly rubbed her forehead.","For some reason...","The conversation had somehow shifted into discussing Noah’s terrible flirting techniques.","She wasn’t even surprised anymore.","A few minutes later, the waiter returned carrying several trays.","Three burgers, slices of freshly baked pizza, and cold drinks were placed neatly on the table.","The delicious aroma instantly filled the air.","Noah smiled.","\"Finally. I’m starving.\"","The three of them enjoyed their meal while chatting about ordinary things, occasionally laughing whenever Arisha teased Noah again or Lyria reacted with another embarrassed expression.","For a little while...","The heavy memories of the recent examination faded into the background.After finishing their meal and paying the bill, they left the restaurant together.","The streets of Novaris City had grown even livelier than before.","People moved between countless shops. Vehicles moved from huge roads.","After walking for several minutes, Noah suddenly stopped.","He looked up at the large sign hanging above one of the buildings.","A smile appeared on his face.","\"Finally... We’re here.\"","Before them stood one of the city’s largest clothing stores, its enormous glass windows displaying elegant suits, dresses, casual outfits, and finely crafted accessories.","Noah folded his arms.","\"It’s been a while since I bought any new clothes. Now it’s time to buy some clothes for this handsome Noah so rich ladies will be charmed by me.\"","\"Delulu,\" Arisha said before walking ahead.","\"What’s ’delulu’?\" Lyria asked with a confused expression.","Arisha sighed. \"It means ’delusional.’ Anyway, let’s go.\""]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: I am Not a Ga-!!","paragraphs":["Inside the clothing store, rows upon rows of neatly arranged outfits stretched in every direction.","Elegant dresses, casual wear, jackets, coats, shoes, and accessories filled the spacious shop. Warm golden lights illuminated the polished wooden floor, while soft instrumental music played quietly in the background.","Dozens of customers wandered through the aisles, browsing the latest designs.","Meanwhile Lyria and Arisha had become completely absorbed in shopping.","Lyria carefully examined every dress she passed, gently running her fingers across the soft fabrics before placing them back if they didn’t suit her taste.","Arisha, on the other hand, walked much more casually. She didn’t seem particularly interested in fashion, but she still picked up outfits from time to time, inspecting them with a thoughtful expression.","Several meters away...","Noah simply watched the two of them.","A helpless smile appeared on his face.","\"As expected...Every woman loves shopping.\"","Lyria suddenly turned around.","In her hands, she held a beautiful maroon dress against the front of her body.","The elegant dress reached just below the knees and featured long sleeves with delicate silver embroidery around the cuffs. The waist was fitted gracefully, while the skirt flowed gently outward.","\"Noah...\"","She looked at him expectantly.","\"How does this one look?\"","Noah observed the dress carefully.","For a brief moment he imagined Lyria wearing it.","Her long golden-blonde hair flowing gently behind her...","Her soft pink eyes her naturally gentle smile...","He nodded honestly.","\"It’ll suit you. You’ll look beautiful in it.\"","Lyria smiled shyly.","\"Really?\"","\"Really.\"","Then Noah glanced around the store.","\"...Actually. Let me choose something for you.\"","Lyria blinked.","\"For... me?\"","She looked genuinely surprised.","Noah simply nodded before walking toward another section of the store.","For some reason he wanted to see the pure and innocent yet mature looking girl wearing something that highlighted her natural elegance.","He carefully browsed through several racks. Eventually, he selected three outfits before returning. Before he could hand them over.","\"What about me?\"","Arisha asked while folding her arms.","\"You aren’t only choosing clothes for Lyria, are you?\"","Noah laughed.","\"Don’t worry. I picked some for you as well.\"","He walked toward another rack.","Unlike Lyria Arisha carried herself with confidence. She looked cool and composed almost all the time.","Rather than soft colors, he searched for outfits that would complement her calm yet slightly playful personality.","A few minutes later...He returned carrying another three sets of clothing. He handed three outfits to Lyria and another three to Arisha.","The two girls looked down at the clothes... Then looked at each other... Before slowly raising their heads to stare at Noah.","\"You actually picked these yourself?\"","Arisha asked.","\"Of course.\"","Noah nodded confidently. \"Now go change into them. I want to see how they look on both of you.\"","The two girls exchanged another glance before walking toward the fitting rooms.","Several minutes later the doors of the first fitting room slowly opened.","Lyria stepped outside.","For a brief moment Noah forgot to speak.","She wore a beautiful ivory-white summer dress with a fitted bodice and a flowing knee-length skirt. Delicate lace decorated the sleeves and collar, while a thin golden ribbon encircled her waist.","The simple elegance of the dress perfectly complemented her long golden-blonde hair and gentle pink eyes.","Her figure was more like mature woman, with beautiful curves.","Under the warm lighting... She almost looked like an angel who had quietly descended into the mortal world.","Lyria nervously smoothed the skirt with both hands.","\"...How is it?\"","Noah smiled softly.","\"It looks perfect. It suits you better than I imagined.\"","Lyria’s cheeks immediately turned pink.","\"Th-Thank you...\"","Just then then door of the second fitting room slid open.","Arisha stepped out with one hand resting on her hip.","Instead of a dress, Noah had chosen something completely different for her.","She wore a fitted black turtleneck tucked neatly into high-waisted dark gray trousers, covered by a short white jacket with silver accents. A thin leather belt emphasized her slender waist, while knee-high black boots completed the outfit.","The modern style highlighted her athletic figure perfectly.","Her long violet hair contrasted beautifully against the white jacket, while her striking golden eyes seemed even brighter than before.","She casually brushed a strand of hair behind her ear.","\"Well? What do you think?\"","Noah looked at her for several seconds before nodding with satisfaction.","\"I was right. That outfit was made for you.\"","A faint smile appeared on Arisha’s lips.","\"...Not bad. I actually like this one. But jacket in summer time... that’s bad idea.\"","She glanced toward Lyria before chuckling.","\"But still it seems you really do have good taste.\"","Lyria nodded in agreement while looking at herself in the nearby mirror.","\"I... I like mine too.\"","Noah folded his arms proudly.","\"I told you.\"","\"Trust my fashion sense.\"","The two girls looked at each other...","Then laughed softly together.","The atmosphere around Noah felt genuinely light again.","The two women disappeared into the fitting rooms once again, each carrying another outfit Noah had picked for them.","While waiting, Noah folded his arms and leaned against one of the clothing racks.","A few customers passed by, occasionally glancing toward the fitting rooms while browsing through neatly arranged summer collections.","He exhaled quietly.","’Am I acting like a good boyfriend? Who chooses outfit for his lover?’ he wondered.","A minute later the doors slid open almost simultaneously.","Noah instinctively looked up.","His eyes widened.","Lyria stepped out first.","She wore a soft sky-blue summer dress that reached just above her knees. The dress featured an off-shoulder neckline that revealed her smooth shoulders and elegant collarbones.","while Arisha, she wore a fitted black sleeveless crop top beneath a light lavender cropped jacket that remained unbuttoned. Combined with high-waisted white shorts and long black thigh-high stockings, the outfit highlighted her toned legs while still maintaining a fashionable summer appearance.","With one hand resting on her hip, she raised an eyebrow.","\"Well?\"","Noah stared at both of them for several seconds.","\"...Beautiful.\"","Lyria lowered her head shyly.","Arisha smirked.","\"I knew it.\" After that they disappearing behind the doors once more.","Several minutes later. They came out again.","This time Noah completely froze.","Lyria stepped out first.","She wore a cream-colored knitted summer top with short sleeves that hugged her figure more closely than her previous outfits. The neckline rested slightly lower than before, subtly accentuating her feminine cleavage without appearing excessive. Her huge chest molded perfectly against her top.","She paired it with a light beige pleated skirt that ended above her knees, exposing her long, fair smooth legs.","Noah could tell her thighs were plump and thick.","She nervously tucked a loose strand of golden hair behind her ear.","\"I-Isn’t this a little... too much?\"","Before Noah could answer.","Arisha walked out.","She had changed into a fitted white sleeveless blouse tucked neatly into dark navy high-waisted shorts.","The shorts hugged her hips perfectly while showing off her long fair athletic legs. Her hips were wide. And Noah could’nt see her back but he could tell she got some big assest there as well.","A thin brown belt completed the outfit, and the blouse’s slightly open collar revealed just enough to make the outfit feel mature without crossing into excess.","Her naturally curvaceous figure became much more noticeable in the modern clothing.","She crossed her arms.","\"So?\"","Noah looked at Lyria.","Then at Arisha.","Then back again.","\"...\"","For the first time that day...","His cheeks actually became slightly warm.","Both girls possessed naturally curvy figures, and these outfits complemented them almost perfectly.","Lyria noticed the faint blush creeping onto Noah’s face.","Her own face immediately turned bright red.","\"H-He blushed...\"","Arisha blinked in surprise before a teasing smile slowly spread across her lips.","\"Oh?\"","She walked a little closer.","\"So even you have your limits.\"","Noah coughed awkwardly.","\"I...\"","He looked away for a moment before meeting their eyes again.","\"...You two look really amazing. But it’s not what you think, okay? I’m not thinking anything inappropriate.\"","His voice carried genuine sincerity.","\"You both honestly look beautiful.\"","Lyria’s pink eyes widened before a sweet smile slowly blossomed across her face.","\"...Thank you.\"","Even Arisha looked momentarily speechless. Then a mischievous grin spread across her face.","\"Look at you, trying your best not to stare at us.\" She folded her arms. \"You’re definitely thinking something bad.\"","Lyria’s eyes widened.","\"N-No, Noah isn’t like that.\"","\"Ahem.\"","Noah cleared his throat before looking at both women with a calm expression.","\"I’m not like other men. I don’t look at you the way they do. Nor do I feel anything for you girls.\"","Arisha studied his face for a few moments before slowly turning toward Lyria.","She leaned closer and whispered loudly enough for Noah to hear.","\"Did you hear him? From the way he’s talking...\" She nodded thoughtfully. \"It appears he’s gay. I mean, he isn’t even attracted to us.\"","\"What the hell?!\"","Noah exclaimed so loudly that a few nearby shoppers turned to look at him.","\"I’m not gay!\"","He said it as though it were the greatest insult he had ever received.","\"Really?\" Arisha asked innocently.","\"But you just said you aren’t attracted to us.\"","\"Hey, come on! Why would I ever say something like that?\" Noah protested immediately. \"Of course I feel attracted to you two, but I can’t just go around saying it!\"","The moment those words left his mouth, a triumphant smile bloomed across Arisha’s face.","\"So I was right.\"","She pointed at him dramatically.","\"You really are a pervert, Noah.\"","Noah clenched his teeth.","After staring at her for several seconds, he simply sighed.","He had already realized there was no winning against her.","Lyria watched the two of them before letting out a soft, amused chuckle.","\"Alright,\" Noah muttered helplessly. \"Let’s just buy them.\"","Both girls nodded happily.","After changing back into their original clothes, they brought the three selected outfits to the counter.","While walking, Lyria looked at Noah.","\"Noah... what about you? Aren’t you buying anything?\"","He shook his head.","\"There’s no need.\"","\"I want to see you wearing some nice clothes,\" Lyria said gently.","\"He’ll definitely look handsome.\" Arisha said further.","\"Hey, I don’t need to—\"","Noah never got the chance to finish.","Both Lyria and Arisha grabbed one of his arms each before dragging him straight toward the men’s clothing section.","---","[A/N: You guys want their images in those three outfits? If yes, then I might try creating them.]"]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: Getting Closer","paragraphs":["After nearly an hour inside the clothing store, Noah finally finished trying on everything.","In the end he had chosen six complete outfits.","Three had been selected by Arisha.","The other three had been picked by Lyria.","Standing in front of the large mirror while changing clothes over and over again had been an oddly new experience for him.","Even stranger the entire time, two beautiful young women had sat nearby, watching him walk out in different outfits before giving their opinions.","\"That color suits you.\"","\"You look much better in this one.\"","\"Try the black jacket.\"","\"No, the white shirt looks better.\"","Each compliment had felt surprisingly genuine.","It had been the first time in his life that any girl had spent so much effort helping him choose clothes.","Noah couldn’t help smiling to himself.","’...It wasn’t bad.’","Eventually, the three of them carried several shopping bags toward the checkout counter.","The cashier began scanning every item one after another.","Beep.","Beep.","Beep.","After a minute, the total appeared on the display.","Noah looked at it. Then looked again.","\"The hell?! Why is it so expensive?!\"","His eyes widened in disbelief.","Arisha glanced at the amount before quietly leaning closer to him.","She lowered her voice so only he could hear.","\"...Noah.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"I think I’ll only buy one outfit.\"","She smiled helplessly. \"This is far too expensive. For my dress, just tell me which one you liked the most out of the three, and I’ll take that one.\"","Noah gave a small nod.","He had been thinking the same thing.","Even buying two outfits, one chosen by Lyria and one by Arisha, would already be stretching his budget.","After all Arisha came from a commoner family.","And Noah although he carried the Eldritch surname, he had long since been exiled from the family.","The allowance he received was nowhere near enough to casually spend such a large amount on clothing.","Just then Lyria stepped beside them.","She looked at both of them before smiling gently.","\"You don’t have to worry.\"","Both Noah and Arisha looked toward her.","\"I’ll pay for everything.\"","Silence fell.","Noah blinked.","\"...Lyria.\"","She smiled warmly.","\"It’s fine.\"","\"No.\"","\"It really is.\"","Arisha sighed before rubbing her forehead. \"Daughter of a duke...\" She laughed softly. \"No wonder this amount is nothing to you.\"","Noah nodded with complete seriousness. \"Lyria is an angel.\"","Arisha immediately agreed. \"Definitely.\"","Lyria’s cheeks turned pink.","\"S-Stop it, you two!\"","Her embarrassed expression only made both of them laugh even harder.","In the end despite Noah insisting several times for giving some money, Lyria refused to let either of them pay.","She quietly settled the entire bill herself before the three of them finally left the clothing store.","By the time they stepped outside, nearly three hours had already passed.","The rest of the afternoon passed peacefully.","They wandered through the bustling streets of Novaris City, visiting small souvenir shops and bookstores before stopping at several roadside stalls.","The aroma of grilled meat, roasted corn, and freshly baked pastries filled the lively streets.","Noah bought grilled skewers while Arisha insisted on trying nearly every snack she came across.","Lyria quietly followed behind them with a gentle smile, occasionally laughing whenever Arisha dragged Noah toward another food stall.","As the afternoon slowly faded. The three eventually arrived at a peaceful park.","Children played happily across the green fields while couples strolled along the stone pathways. A cool breeze rustled through the trees.","The atmosphere felt calm.","Noah found himself genuinely enjoying the moment.","By the time they began walking back toward the academy, the sky had already turned orange. The setting sun painted the entire campus with warm golden light.","The gentle evening breeze carried the scent of blooming flowers through the stone pathways.","Noah walked quietly between them.","\"...Today was nice,\" he muttered.","Neither of the girls spoke immediately.","The peaceful silence felt surprisingly comforting.","After a few moments, Lyria slowly stepped a little closer to him.","She lowered her gaze toward the stone path. \"...I’ll miss you two.\"","Noah looked at her. He smiled sheepishly. \"True. I will miss you two as well.\"","Then he chuckled softly. \"Hah... my days back home are probably going to be incredibly boring.\"","Lyria looked up at him. \"You can call me from time to time.\"","Her smile grew warmer. \"We can just... talk.\"","Noah smiled. \"Of course. I’ll even video call you.\"","Lyria giggled.","\"I’ll be waiting.\"","\"Hey.\" Arisha folded her arms dramatically. \"Don’t forget about me.\"","Noah laughed. \"As if I could.\"","\"Hmph.\"","She nodded in satisfaction.","\"Good answer.\"","For a while, the three continued walking beneath the orange sky.","Then Arisha suddenly moved closer. Without warning, she slipped her arm through Noah’s and held his hand.","His body stiffened slightly.","\"W-What are you doing?\"","She looked at him with an amused smile. \"So...How does it feel?\"","Noah blinked.","\"...How does what feel? I mean...\"","Her teasing expression softened. \"You were completely down.\"","She looked ahead as they walked.","\"But now...it seems like you’re finally smiling again. Genuinely.\"","Noah fell silent. He hadn’t even realized it himself.","After a long moment. A small, genuine smile slowly appeared on his face. He’s hand slowly intertwined with her.","\"...Thank you.\"","He looked forward at the road stretching toward the academy.","\"...Thank you... both of you.\"","Lyria smiled softly.","Arisha simply squeezed his hand. Her ears turned into soft shade of pink.","Lyria was oblivious to this.","The three of them continued walking side by side beneath the golden evening sky, their shadows stretching across the stone pathway as the academy gates slowly came into view.","They were growing closer to Noah slowly.","---","Meanwhile, back at the academy.","Inside the training hall, Damien sat on the floor, exhausted and drenched in sweat after another grueling training session with Morgana.","\"You did well today.\"","\"Thank you, Master,\" Damien replied, breathing heavily.","Morgana gave a slight nod.","\"Anyway, enjoy this remaining month with your family. Next month, we will be visiting the Duchy of Thornveil.\"","\"Thornveil?\" Damien asked in surprise. \"You mean the duchy where Ophelia is from?\"","---","[A/N:] Shit, I kept writing and writing, and I just couldn’t stop. Sorry for stretching this date for so many Chapters. Tch! The sad thing is, you guys will never get the chance to go on a date with two beautiful ladies... well, neither will I. Sigh... At least I can write it in a novel.]"]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: Back To Home","paragraphs":["Back at the Academy","Noah stood in front of the mirror one last time before leaving his dormitory.","He wore a fitted white T-shirt beneath a black leather jacket, paired with dark jeans and black boots. The casual outfit suited him surprisingly well, making his snow-white hair and glacier-blue eyes stand out even more.","He adjusted the collar of his jacket before smiling faintly.","\"Not bad.\"","Thanks to Heart of Absolute Frost, he no longer had to worry about the summer heat. Although he could still feel warmth, it no longer affected him. Even if he stood beneath the scorching sun all day in desert, his body remained comfortably cool.","His gaze shifted toward the bed.","Nancy lay curled into a small black ball of fur, lazily watching him with half-open golden eyes.","\"No, let’s go.\"","He picked up his travel bag before looking at the cat.","\"It’s time to visit my... ex-home.\"","\"Meow?\"","Nancy tilted her head in confusion. She had absolutely no idea what this strange human was talking about.","Noah had never discussed traveling anywhere with her. He crouched before her and smiled.","\"I can’t leave you here alone.\"","Nancy blinked.","\"Who would take care of you?\"","\"Meow! Meow!\"","She immediately protested. Her cries almost sounded as though she were saying,","’I was taking care of myself perfectly fine before I met you!’","Unfortunately for her, Noah had no intention of listening.","\"Don’t argue.\"","Nancy narrowed her eyes.","\"Meow—!\"","Before she could finish protesting, Noah scooped her up with one arm.","\"I mean... let’s go.\"","The cat continued grumbling beneath her breath. Sadly her opinion carried very little weight.","Morning sunlight illuminated the academy grounds. The campus had become much quieter now that the summer vacation had begun.","As Noah stepped out of the dormitory building with Nancy resting comfortably in his arm, two familiar figures immediately caught his attention.","Lyria and Arisha were already waiting near the entrance.","Lyria wore a simple cream-colored summer dress beneath a light cardigan, while her long golden-blonde hair flowed gently in the morning breeze.","Beside her, Arisha wore a black fitted T-shirt beneath a light gray jacket, paired with dark jeans that complemented her cool demeanor perfectly. Her long violet hair had been tied into a high ponytail.","Both girls looked toward Noah.","\"Good morning, guys.\"","Lyria smiled warmly before waving.","\"Good morning, Noah.\"","Arisha was just about to greet him as well.","\"He—\"","Her words suddenly stopped.","Her eyes locked onto the creature resting comfortably in Noah’s arm.","\"...N-Noah?\"","She blinked.","\"...That cat?\"","Lyria also noticed Nancy.","Her pink eyes sparkled with excitement.","\"Noah! You have a cat? And you never told us? It’s so cute!\"","Noah laughed awkwardly.","\"Haha... I wanted to tell you both.\"","He rubbed the back of his neck.","\"But I never really got the chance. And honestly...It’s just a cat. Her name is Nancy.\"","Arisha slowly narrowed her eyes.","\"...That’s the same cat. The one I tried to pet about a month ago. But she never let me touch her.\"","She looked directly into Noah’s eyes.","\"Since when has she been your pet?\"","Nancy immediately frowned.","Yes. The cat genuinely frowned. She clearly disliked being referred to as someone’s pet.","Unfortunately she couldn’t exactly argue.","Noah smiled nervously. \"I found her before our written examinations.\"","He thought for a moment.","\"It was the same day you, Regnar, and Draven taught me.\"","The moment he finished speaking...","Arisha’s expression turned noticeably colder.","Lyria, meanwhile, had absolutely no idea why Arisha suddenly looked upset.","\"So...\"","Arisha folded her arms.","\"The reason you acted so strangely back then, it was because of her?\"","Noah nodded honestly.","\"Yes.\"","\"Damn you, Noah!\"","She marched straight toward him. Within seconds, she stood directly in front of him.","Noah couldn’t help smiling helplessly. He knew exactly how much Arisha loved cute things despite always acting like an indifferent ice queen.","\"Hey. I told you now.\"","He gently lifted Nancy slightly.","\"If you want... You can pet her.\"","Arisha looked at the cat.","Then at Noah. Before she could respond, Lyria stepped forward first.","\"Really?\"","She smiled brightly.","\"Then let me.\"","She carefully extended her hand toward Nancy.","The cat flinched. She was fully prepared to hiss.","Unfortunately Noah’s free hand gently held her in place.","\"Behave. Be a good girl.\"","\"Meow!!\"","Nancy protested indignantly. Yet she could do absolutely nothing.","Lyria gently stroked her soft black fur.","\"So fluffy...\"","She smiled happily. At that exact moment...","Arisha calmly raised her own hand.","Instead of petting the cat, she placed it atop Noah’s snow-white hair.","Then she gently began stroking it.","Noah immediately blushed.","\"H-Hey! You’re doing it again!\"","Lyria froze.","She slowly withdrew her hand from Nancy before looking toward Arisha with wide eyes.","Arisha merely smirked.","\"This is your punishment.\"","She continued patting his hair.","\"For hiding such an adorable cat from me.\"","She looked at Noah with obvious amusement.","\"...Although. I actually prefer patting you rather than Nancy.\"","She finally withdrew her hand.","Lyria continued staring at them.","Her cheeks gradually turned pink. She quietly looked down at her own hand...","Then toward Noah’s head.","For some reason she suddenly wanted to try it too. The thought embarrassed her enough that she immediately looked away.","Arisha casually adjusted her jacket.","\"Anyway. We should leave. My train departs in half an hour.\"","\"Oh, right. Shit.\"","Noah started following after her.","\"Lyria. Let’s go.\"","She snapped out of her thoughts.","\"O-Okay.\"","Still blushing faintly, she hurried after the two of them.","---","BEEP!","A bright flash of light filled the teleportation chamber.","Moments later Noah stepped out of the portal. A cool breeze immediately greeted him.","He slowly looked around.","\"The weather here isn’t nearly as hot as Novaris City...\"","He smiled faintly.","\"...Though I suppose it doesn’t matter anymore.\"","\"Meow~\"","Nancy lazily stretched inside his arm before looking around curiously. Her bright yellow eyes carefully observed everything surrounding them.","Noah gently scratched beneath her chin.","\"We’re home.\"","He paused.","\"...Well. Can I really call this place home anymore?\"","A complicated smile crossed his face. Unlike most students, Noah had returned through a teleportation gate. The academy certainly wasn’t generous enough to provide free long-distance portal access for every student.","Fortunately his elder brother, Nathan, had already arranged everything beforehand. Without Nathan’s help, Noah would have spent long time traveling by train like Arisha.","Lyria, on the other hand, had naturally returned to her duchy through a teleportation gate as well.","Leaving the teleportation station behind, Noah entered the capital city of the Eldritch Duchy.","Gelidra City.","The duchy occupied the northern region of the empire. Every winter, heavy snowfall blanketed nearly the entire territory.","Farther north, beyond the last settlements where civilization ended, stretched endless frozen lands covered in snow throughout almost the entire year.","Beyond those icy coasts, across the northern sea, lay Glaciara—the Frozen Continent.","The second-largest continent in the world. A land where eternal snowstorms ruled. Gelidra itself presented an unusual sight.","The city perfectly blended modern civilization with ancient aristocratic elegance.","Glass office buildings and sleek commercial districts stood beside towering Gothic cathedrals that had endured for centuries.","Modern trams glided through wide stone-paved avenues, while elegant horse-drawn carriages still traveled the older districts.","The central city bustled with modern architecture. Yet the noble quarter retained its centuries-old identity.","Magnificent stone mansions, medieval fortifications, towering Gothic estates, stained-glass windows, wrought-iron gates, and narrow cobblestone streets created an atmosphere unlike anywhere else.","It reminded Noah of several cities from his previous world.","\"...Edinburgh, Prague or perhaps London.\"","None matched perfectly.","Instead Gelidra felt like a seamless fusion of all three.","It was ancient, modern, elegant and powerful.","Noah slowly walked through the city instead of hiring a carriage. He wanted to enjoy the scenery.","\"Meow~\"","Nancy quietly watched everything with endless curiosity from his arm.","\"It’s beautiful...\"","Noah muttered softly. Nearly half an hour later he finally stopped walking.","His eyes slowly rose upward. Before him stood an enormous manor surrounded by towering iron gates and perfectly maintained gardens.","The estate resembled something taken directly from an old European aristocratic painting.","Gray stone walls, countless gothic windows and elegant balconies, everything radiated dignity and prestige.","Noah smiled helplessly. \"I inherited memories of this place...\"","He looked at the grand mansion in silence.","\"...But seeing it with my own eyes. It really feels like I’ve stepped into the medieval era.\"","After taking a slow breath, he finally stood before the gates of the place that had once been his home."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Meeting His Family","paragraphs":["Noah walked toward the gate. The guards stationed at the entrance noticed him immediately.","Surprise flashed across their faces before they bowed respectfully and opened the massive iron gates.","\"Welcome back, Young Master Noah.\"","Noah nodded politely and stepped inside the estate.","His blue eyes wandered across the familiar surroundings.","The elegant gardens were as immaculate as ever, colorful flowers blooming beneath the warm morning sun while stone pathways stretched toward the grand manor standing proudly at the center of the estate.","He walked through the entrance and into the spacious main hall.","The interior was just as luxurious as he remembered.","Polished marble floors reflected the light pouring in through the tall windows.","Expensive paintings decorated the walls, while crystal chandeliers hung from the high ceiling.","He looked around curiously.","’Where is everyone?’","Just then, slow footsteps echoed through the hall.","An elderly man dressed in a perfectly tailored butler’s uniform approached him with dignified steps.","His neatly combed gray hair and gentle wrinkles gave him an air of wisdom and kindness.","The moment he reached Noah, he bowed respectfully.","\"It is truly good to see you again after so many months, Young Master Noah.\"","A small smile appeared on Noah’s face.","\"It is good to see you too, Uncle Theon.\"","The old butler smiled warmly before straightening his posture.","\"Young Master Nathan has been waiting for your arrival.\"","\"Really?\" Noah asked. \"Where is my brother?\"","\"He is currently inside his chamber.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Alright. I’ll go there myself.\"","Theon bowed once more.","\"As you wish, Young Master.\"","The elderly butler quietly stepped aside while Noah walked deeper into the manor.","---","After a short walk through the long corridor, Noah stopped in front of a large wooden door.","He raised his hand and knocked.","Knock.","Knock.","A few moments later, the door slowly opened.","Standing there was a handsome young man around twenty-six years old.","He possessed light wheat-blond hair, sharp purple eyes, and a well-built physique that reflected years of disciplined training.","The moment he saw Noah, a broad smile spread across his face.","\"Noah! You’re finally here.\"","Before Noah could respond, Nathan stepped forward and wrapped him in a firm hug.","Noah smiled faintly before returning the embrace.","\"It’s good to see you too, Brother.\"","He lightly patted Nathan’s broad back.","Unfortunately someone else happened to be trapped between the two brothers.","\"Meooow!!\"","Nancy was squeezed tightly between them, desperately struggling to breathe.","Nathan immediately released Noah.","\"Oh.\"","The poor black cat remained limp in Noah’s arms, breathing heavily as though she had barely survived a life-threatening battle.","Noah couldn’t help chuckling.","Nathan scratched the back of his head awkwardly.","\"Sorry...\"","His gaze then fell on Nancy once more. His eyebrows rose in surprise.","\"You have a cat?\"","Noah nodded.","\"Yeah. I took her in some time ago.\"","Nathan slowly extended his hand.","\"Can I pet her?\"","The instant his fingers moved closer.","\"Hissss!\"","Nancy bared her tiny fangs and hissed angrily.","Nathan immediately withdrew his hand.","\"...Seems like she doesn’t like me.\"","Noah laughed softly.","\"She’s a little picky.\"","Nathan sighed helplessly.","\"I can see that.\"","After a brief silence, Noah asked,","\"Where’s Father?\"","Nathan replied,","\"He should be inside his study.\"","\"And Mother?\"","He wondered where his mother might be.","But he knew that his brother must have informed their father of his return home.","Nathan smiled somewhat awkwardly.","\"She is probably sitting on her balcony, reading another book.\"","Noah blinked before nodding.","\"I see.\"","He looked toward the corridor.","\"Well then... I should go and greet them.\"","Nathan’s lips curved into a knowing smirk.","\"Sure.\"","He folded his arms.","\"Go ahead.\"","Noah looked at him strangely.","\"Wait... you’re not coming?\"","Nathan immediately shook his head.","\"No.\"","A grin spread across his face.","\"Why should I come? This is your battle.\"","Noah stared at him speechlessly.","Nathan chuckled.","\"Besides, I think Father will be very pleased after hearing about your progress at the academy.\"","Noah nodded slowly.","\"I hope so.\"","He turned toward the door.","\"Well then... I’ll go meet Father first.\"","Nathan gave him a thumbs-up. He tried to encourage his brother.","\"Best of luck.\"","\"Thanks.\" Noah had no choice but thank Nathan and leave.","With that, Noah left Nathan’s chamber and walked through the quiet corridors of the manor.","His destination was clear.","The study room was where his father, Julian Eldritch, usually handled his work.","Soon, Noah stood before the heavy wooden door.","He took a deep breath.","The man inside was not the father from his previous life...","He was Noah’s father.","The father of the original owner of this body.","Yet now, Noah possessed all of Noah Eldritch’s memories.","Who knew... maybe there’s some twist in my life story, and I was actually the real Noah from the very beginning?","Reading countless web novels had led him to such absurd conclusions.","For now, however, he pushed those thoughts aside.","He raised his hand and knocked on the door.","\"Come in.\"","A cold, authoritative voice came from the other side.","Noah slowly pushed the door open.","The spacious study came into view.","A large wooden desk stood near the center of the room, covered with neatly organized documents. Behind it sat Julian Eldritch.","He possessed silver hair and deep purple eyes.","Noah had inherited his father’s silver hair, while his older brother had inherited those striking purple eyes.","For a brief moment, Noah didn’t know what to say.","If it had been his father from his previous life.","He would have simply smiled and said, ’Dad, I’m back.’","But here, what was he supposed to say?","According to Noah’s memories, their relationship had always been somewhat distant.","He couldn’t greet him so casually.","He bowed respectfully. \"Greetings, Father. It’s me, Noah... I’m back.\"","He tried to be calm as much as possible.","The cat in his hand also sense the man in front of them.","He was no ordinary person. As head of the Eldritch family, he was really strong.","A man who was at Astral core rank, at high stage. Making him one of the powerhouse of the empire.","Julian, who had been reading a document, stopped and slowly raised his head.","His calm eyes studied Noah for several long seconds.","Then he spoke in heavy voice.","\"Come. Have a seat.\"","Noah walked forward and sat on the chair opposite him.","Julian leaned back against his chair.","\"You have changed a lot, Noah.\"","His sharp gaze remained fixed on him.","\"Just by looking into your eyes, I could tell... the foolishness that once existed there has vanished.\"","His voice remained calm, carrying the natural authority expected of the Duke of the Eldritch Duchy.","Noah quietly nodded.","\"And I heard about your performance during your first semester.\"","A faint smile appeared on Julian’s face.","\"You did well... far better than I had ever expected.\"","His voice was genuine. He was truly satisfied and happy with his son’s progress.","The same young man who used to spend his all day in entertainment.","At that time he didn’t mind much since Noah didn’t possess high potential. So he decided let him enjoy his life.","And that was their mistake.","\"Thank you, Father,\" Noah replied respectfully.","Julian continued observing him for another moment.","\"...You are far too calm.\"","Noah remained silent.","’What am I supposed to say? I honestly have no idea...’","Julian watched him quietly before speaking again.","\"I also heard about what happened during your academy examination. You nearly lost your life while fighting a demon. You stood your ground despite overwhelming odds.\"","\"Yes...\" Noah answered calmly. \"...But it wasn’t that difficult.\"","A small smile appeared on Julian’s face.","\"You did well, Noah.\"","His voice became softer.","\"For the first time in many years... I felt proud of you, my son.\"","Noah didn’t know why. But hearing those words filled a part of his heart with warmth.","He felt relief and happiness. Despite he didn’t want to feel it.","Emotions he hadn’t expected.","\"Meow.\"","The black cat resting comfortably on his lap let out a quiet meow.","Julian merely glanced at Nancy before returning his attention to Noah.","He remained silent for a moment before speaking again.","\"And...How are you? You went through a great deal throughout your first semester. Since the first incident in academy, then that dungeon incident then at Oakhaven city...and now this.\"","He continued further with sligt sad tone.\"...Yet I never even called to ask whether you were alright. But I always kept tap on your progress.\"","A trace of guilt surfaced in his eyes.","\"I am truly sorry for that, Noah. But everything I did... was for your own good. Seeing you finally grow into the man you were meant to become...has made me happier than you can imagine.\"","Julian slowly stood from his chair.","He walked around the desk until he stood beside Noah.","Then he gently placed a hand on his shoulder.","\"Welcome back, Noah.\"","Throughout the entire conversation, Noah hadn’t known how to react.","He hadn’t known what to say. But one thing was certain. Hearing those words from his father.","Or perhaps, from Noah’s father. It no longer mattered. He was Noah now."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: Mother (1)","paragraphs":["Noah now stood in front of his mother’s chamber.","Honestly, he wished he had simply waited and spoken with everyone together during lunch.","He took a slow breath before raising his hand.","Knock.","Knock.","For several moments, there was no response from inside.","Then, a calm voice finally reached his ears.","\"Come in.\"","Hearing her permission, Noah slowly pushed the door open.","The spacious chamber came into view.","It was the master bedroom shared by his parents.","The room was elegantly furnished, with polished wooden furniture, luxurious carpets, and tall windows that allowed warm sunlight to pour inside.","Beyond them lay a wide balcony overlooking the vast gardens of the manor.","A woman sat quietly on a chair placed near the balcony.","Her back faced Noah.","Her long wheat-blond hair flowed freely down her back, shimmering beneath the afternoon light.","Nathan had inherited that beautiful hair color from their mother.","Noah quietly walked toward her.","Stopping a few steps behind, he spoke softly.","\"Mother... I’m back.\"","Those simple words left his lips as he silently prepared himself for whatever response awaited him.","Among everyone in the family...","She had been the angriest with him.","She had known that Noah had committed everything while heavily intoxicated and that Ophelia had used the incident to portray herself as the victim.","Even so she had remained furious.","At least, that was what Noah believed.","He remembered countless occasions when she had patiently tried to correct him.","She had repeatedly warned him to stay away from bad habits.","Most of her concern had centered around his reckless lifestyle.","Drinking alcohol from the early age of sixteen.","Sneaking out with wealthy friends to attend extravagant parties.","Ignoring his sword training. Neglecting his responsibilities.","In the beginning, she hadn’t said much. It had only happened occasionally.","But as the years passed those habits had gradually become more frequent.","Then came that incident.","The final straw that had shattered her patience.","Noah still didn’t truly know what had angered her the most.","Was it because he had attempted to force himself upon a woman?","As a woman herself, such an act would naturally be unforgivable.","Or was it because he had brought immense disgrace upon the Eldritch family?","While Noah remained lost in his thoughts, the woman quietly closed the book resting in her hands.","She rose gracefully from her chair, the folds of her dark navy-blue gown settling elegantly around her figure.","Then she slowly turned around.","Cold blue eyes, clear and tranquil like the frozen lakes of winter, met Noah’s.","She was Catelyn Eldritch.","The daughter of Lord Branjen, one of the great noble houses that governed the northern region of the Eldritch Duchy. A land where winter reigned throughout the entire year.","Her porcelain-smooth skin remained flawless.","Despite being a woman in her late forties, she possessed the youthful elegance of someone in her early thirties.","Time seemed to have treated her with remarkable kindness.","\"You’ve returned...\"","Her voice was calm.","She began walking toward Noah with slow, graceful steps.","Her heels clicked softly against the polished wooden floor.","Her cold blue eyes never left him, carefully observing every change in her son.","She didn’t focus on the cat. She was ignored once again.","Soon, she stopped directly before him.","Even with her high heels, she was still slightly shorter than Noah.","He had grown to nearly one hundred eighty-four centimeters, well over six feet tall.","Silence settled between the two. Neither of them spoke.","Several long moments passed.","Then Catelyn slowly raised her gloved hand. Her delicate fingers gently cupped Noah’s cheek.","His blue eyes widened in surprise. The icy expression on her face softened ever so slightly.","\"How have you been... my son?\"","Her voice was warm and gentle.","Just as it had been a year ago.","\"I’m doing well... better than ever.\"","Catelyn studied his eyes carefully.","A small smile gradually appeared on her face.","Without another word, she stepped forward and wrapped her arms around him.","\"My boy... I’m sorry for being so harsh on you for so long.\"","Her voice came softly as she held him close.","Unfortunately Nancy once again found herself trapped between two giants.","\"Meow...\"","The poor black cat let out a pitiful cry of protest.","Noah blinked in surprise, unable to understand why she was apologizing.","The huge felt warm and gentle. Reminding him of his true mother from mast life.","From time to time he truly miss them. Wondering if there was any chance to go back.","While in this world his parents were not close to him.","At least that was he considered.","But now when she hugged him... he felt calm and nice.","His father Julian and mother Catelyn... bith of them genuinely care about him even now.","Though he does think that what Noah had done had deserved that kind of treatment.","Yet his mother genuinely regretted the way she had treated him.","\"Mother... why are you apologizing? Of course because I treated you so coldly for all these months.\"","She gently loosened the embrace before looking into his eyes.","\"I refused to let you return home or even galk to you. But I had to do it. So that you could learn to live on your own. That you could grow up...And leave behind those terrible habits.\"","She slowly released him completely.","\"If I had continued treating you as before, you would have kept begging for forgiveness and asking me to bring you back home.\"","She shook her head gently.","\"I didn’t want that. So I forced myself to be harsh. Your father did the same. I wanted you to finally mature.\"","She smiled faintly.","\"Honestly... it could have gone either way. You might have become an even greater wayward or a better man. Thankfully...The latter happened.\"","She looked at Noah from head to toe before smiling proudly.","\"Just look at you. You’ve changed completely. You finally look like a proper gentleman.\"","Noah once again found himself speechless.","How would they react if they ever discovered that I wasn’t the original Noah...?","That thought surfaced once more.","But only briefly. He had already accepted his decision. He was Noah now.","Nothing would change that.","A gentle smile appeared on his face.","\"I understand, Mother. So please don’t apologize. I’m not angry. If anything... This experience helped me grow.\"","As soon as those words left his mouth, Catelyn’s blue eyes widened slightly.","\"You truly have changed...\"","She looked at him with visible surprise.","\"I don’t remember you ever speaking so gently and nicely.\"","Noah smiled awkwardly and rubbed the back of his neck.","\"Well...I learned many things during these months while living in exile.\"","She nodded proudly.","\"Come. Sit with me.\"","She led him toward a long sofa inside the room.","The two of them sat beside one another. The cat rested on his lap."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: Mother (2)","paragraphs":["\"My dear, I know what you’ve gone through during these past months.\"","She folded her hands neatly on her lap.","\"We always kept track of your life. First six months were normal. But after this new year, I was terrified every time I heard that you had found yourself in another dangerous situation.\"","Her expression turned worried.","\"How could one person go through so much in only four months?\"","Noah laughed helplessly.","\"Haha...I don’t know. My luck must simply be terrible.\"","He couldn’t help saying that. Ever since he had arrived in this world...","Only four months had passed. Yet those months had felt unbelievably long.","\"So many things happened. Many near-death experiences...\"","Catelyn looked at him with gentle eyes.","\"But I’m grateful you’re safe. You survived every one of them.\"","She smiled proudly.","\"And now you’ve already reached the High Rank of the Awakened Core Realm. Your growth has been astonishing. Even your brother didn’t grow so fast.\"","Noah nodded.","\"That’s true. Those incidents forced me beyond my limits.\"","Catelyn wasn’t merely the graceful wife of a Duke. She was an exceptionally powerful mage herself.","An Aeternum Core mage. At high core stage.","Moreover she specialized in Ice Magic.","Just like Noah.","’I can finally learn from her.’","Back then, Noah always avoided her lessons. But not anymore. Looks like my summer vacation is going to be busy.","Swordsmanship with Father and Nathan...","Magic lessons with Mother.","His thoughts drifted as Catelyn’s gaze shifted toward the black cat resting comfortably on his lap.","\"Is she your new pet?\"","A trace of surprise appeared on her face.","\"That’s unexpected. You never liked cats or dogs before.\"","Noah smiled.","\"Well, I changed. I found her injured at the academy. I decided to help her. And somehow... I grew fond of how cute she was.\"","Catelyn smiled gently.","\"Hmm. She truly is adorable.\"","She reached out and gently stroked Nancy’s soft black fur.","Surprisingly this time, the cat didn’t hiss.","Nancy merely narrowed her golden eyes before lazily allowing herself to be petted.","After a brief silence Catelyn spoke again.","\"Now, about Ophelia.\"","The moment that name was mentioned. The atmosphere changed slightly.","Ophelia.","His former fiancée. The woman he had once tried to harass and got exile.","Noah looked at his mother. \"What about her?\"","Catelyn observed his expression carefully.","\"Do you still love her?\"","His brows immediately furrowed. As if he was greatly displeased by those words. There wasn’t even the slightest hesitation.","He slowly shook his head.","\"No. I don’t love her. Not even a little.\"","Catelyn quietly studied his expression for another moment before nodding.","\"That’s good to hear. Although what you did was undeniably wrong. She also turned the matter into a far greater spectacle than it needed to be.\"","She sighed softly.","\"I’m relieved you’ve let her go.\"","Then she asked,","\"How do you deal with her at the academy? You two are classmates, after all.\"","Noah answered calmly.","\"We don’t speak to each other. We both avoid one another whenever possible.\"","\"Good. Very good.\"","A satisfied smile appeared on Catelyn’s face.","\"Don’t worry, my dear. Now that you’ve become a better man...And such a handsome young gentleman...I’m certain you’ll meet someone far better.\"","She smiled teasingly.","\"I’ll personally find the perfect young lady for you. Someone far more beautiful than Ophelia.\"","Noah smirked.","For some reason the faces of Arisha and Lyria suddenly appeared in his mind.","Both of them were undeniably more beautiful than Ophelia.","Then he frowned.","’Damn! Why am I thinking about those two?’","He quickly shook the thought away.","\"Mother...I think you should worry about finding someone for Brother Nathan first. He’s already twenty-six. And he still doesn’t have a fiancée. I know people don’t marry as early these days... But he doesn’t even have a lover. I think we should be more concerned about him first.\"","Catelyn immediately nodded.","\"You’re right. I’ve tried speaking to him countless times. But he refuses to listen. When I told him to at least try to get closer to women and find someone he could love... even then, he didn’t listen to me and refused to do so.\"","She sighed helplessly before smiling nostalgically.","\"Do you know, your father was twenty-five and I was twenty-three when we got married.\"","\"I know, I know. But you two loved each other and decided to get married. Brother still hasn’t found a woman he loves,\" Noah replied.","\"That’s true.\" Catelyn nodded thoughtfully. \"Love has no age. He might find some one later. But young people naturally tend to find someone they could date. Since they are more interested in those kind of stuff... yet your brother never has.\"","Her blue eyes shifted toward Noah.","\"What about you? Have you found someone you like at the academy?\"","Noah was taken aback by the sudden question.","\"Me?\"","Once again, the images of two young women flashed through his mind.","He quickly shook his head.","\"No, Mother. I haven’t.\"","Catelyn narrowed her eyes suspiciously.","\"For some reason, I feel like you’re not being entirely honest.\"","She smiled faintly.","\"But you’re still young. If you are feeling something for a woman, then what you’re feeling might simply be attraction rather than love. You might be confused.\"","\"Yes, Mother. You’re right. It’s just attraction. Not a crush or anything.\" He replied immediately.","\"Good.\"","She nodded in satisfaction before asking another question.","\"So... who is this girl that attracted you?\"","Noah inwardly cursed.","’Dammit!’","\"Mother... there isn’t anyone.\"","\"Oh, come on now.\"","She folded her arms with an amused smile.","\"You just admitted it was only attraction. And I’m your mother. I can tell you’re lying just by looking at your face.\"","Noah sighed helplessly.","\"I guess I can’t hide anything from you.\"","He smiled slightly before saying,","\"Well... there is one woman who interests me.\"","Curiosity immediately appeared in Catelyn’s eyes.","\"And who might she be?\"","Noah’s smile widened.","\"She’s Morgana Celestine. The head instructor of my class.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, the reaction on his mother’s face was exactly what he had hoped to see.","’That’s a nice reaction.’ He thought.","Unfortunately for him after that joke, Noah ended up being scolded by his mother for quite a while.","---","[A/N: Keke! Sorry, guys, I decided not to include any family drama. I was too tired to write it, so I dropped that idea. Haha!]"]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Family Dinner","paragraphs":["Finally, Noah returned to his bedroom.","He gently placed Nancy on the large bed before looking around the room.","\"My room is still clean.\"","His gaze slowly swept across the chamber.","Everything looked exactly the same as it had before he left the manor nearly ten months ago.","The neatly arranged bookshelf. The polished wooden furniture.","The large bed and even the curtains remained unchanged.","Nothing seemed out of place.","A small smile appeared on his face. \"Good.\"","He sat down on the edge of the bed beside Nancy. Slowly, he reached out and gently stroked her head.","The black cat frowned slightly in protest.","Still she made no attempt to move away.","If anything, she quietly leaned into his hand, clearly enjoying the gentle petting despite trying not to show it.","Noah chuckled.","\"Such a tsundere.\"","His fingers continued brushing through her soft black fur.","Then the color of her fur reminded him of someone.","Mary.","\"...Damn.\"","The smile on his face gradually disappeared.","He had been doing everything he could to move forward.","Most of his time had been occupied with training. Or spending time with other people.","Whenever he kept himself busy. He hardly thought about her.","But whenever he found himself alone. Her memory quietly returned.","Just as it always did.","He rubbed his forehead tiredly.","\"Looks like...it’s going to take a little longer.\"","Nancy quietly looked at him before resting her head against his thigh.","Noah simply continued stroking her soft fur in silence.","---","Night arrived before Noah even realized it.","The dining hall was brightly illuminated by elegant crystal chandeliers hanging from the ceiling.","A long dining table stood at the center of the room, covered with an immaculate white tablecloth and an assortment of luxurious dishes.","The Eldritch family had finally gathered together.","Julian sat at the head of the table. Across from him, on his right, sat Catelyn. Nathan occupied the seat to Julian’s left.","Meanwhile, Noah sat beside Nathan.","The atmosphere remained calm as everyone quietly enjoyed dinner.","After a while, Julian placed down his knife and fork before looking toward Noah.","\"Your reputation at the academy has improved considerably.\"","His voice remained calm and authoritative.","\"I’ve even had several noble families personally tell me how much you’ve changed.\"","Noah nodded politely.","\"I’m glad to hear that.\"","\"I’ll continue working hard.\"","\"I’ll perform even better during the next semester.\"","Julian gave a satisfied nod.","Then Catelyn suddenly remembered something.","\"Now that I think about it...\"","She looked at Noah curiously.","\"What happened to your semester results?\"","\"Did you receive them?\"","Julian’s attention also shifted toward his younger son.","\"Indeed.\"","\"I never asked.\"","\"Did the academy release the rankings?\"","\"Yes.\"","Noah nodded calmly.","\"I already received them.\"","Nathan smiled.","\"Oh?\"","\"That’s good.\"","\"So...\"","\"What rank did you obtain?\"","Noah smiled faintly before answering as though it were nothing unusual.","\"I ranked second.\"","Silence.","The entire dining hall became deathly quiet.","Even Theon, who stood respectfully beside the table waiting to serve the family, couldn’t hide the surprise on his face.","Catelyn blinked several times.","\"...Did I hear that correctly?\"","Nathan slowly turned toward Noah.","His eyes had widened in disbelief.","\"Little brother...\"","\"...you’re joking, right?\"","Even Julian remained silent.","His expression barely changed. Yet anyone who knew him could tell, the Duke wasn’t speaking because he was still processing what Noah had just said.","Noah sighed helplessly.","\"Seriously...\"","He pulled out his phone.","Opening the academy application, he navigated to his student profile before placing the phone on the table.","\"See for yourselves.\"","Everyone leaned forward.","Their eyes immediately landed on Noah’s profile.","First-Year Academic Ranking: Rank 2","His previous ranking...","1786","Had completely disappeared.","In its place...","Only one number remained.","Rank 2.","Noah clicked his tongue.","\"Tch...\"","\"I would’ve taken first place...\"","\"...if Damien Ashworth hadn’t broken through to the Condensed Core Realm.\"","His tone carried a trace of dissatisfaction.","Despite everything...","He had once again finished behind Damien.","Still at least he had surpassed every other student in the first year.","Kaelan had also reached the High Rank of the Awakened Core Realm.","However, he had only broken through recently.","Lyria, Arisha, Leonard and Emm. All of them remained at the Mid Rank of the Awakened Core Realm.","Noah had firmly secured second place.","\"...This...\"","Catelyn stared blankly at the phone before suddenly looking back at Noah.","\"Oh my... Oh my goodness, Noah!\"","The cold and composed noble lady completely forgot to maintain her elegant demeanor.","Joy overflowed across her face.","She smiled proudly.","\"You’ve exceeded every expectation.\"","Nathan laughed softly.","\"That’s amazing, little brother. When I was a first-year student... I wasn’t even among the top five! Even I never achieved something like this during my first semester.\"","He shook his head in admiration.","\"You’ve really worked hard.\"","Then a loud laugh echoed throughout the dining hall.","\"Hahaha!\"","Julian laughed openly, something that happened only on rare occasions.","\"This...was completely unexpected.\"","He looked at Noah with unconcealed pride.","\"I remember telling you to at least aim for the top ten.\"","A smile remained on his face. \"I only said that to motivate you...I never imagined...that you would actually finish your first semester ranked second in the entire academy.\"","\"True. Instructor Morgana really helped me a lot. She’s an amazing teacher.\" Noah said.","\"Oh, her. I know Morgana well,\" Julian said with a nod of understanding. \"She is an S-Rank Hero from the Celestine Household. A true genius with extraordinary talent.\"","\"So, Father... you also think she’s amazing?\"","\"Of course.\" Julian nodded calmly. \"I have a great deal of respect for her. Despite her young age, she has already reached such a remarkable rank. Very few people can achieve what she has.\"","Catelyn suddenly frowned.","\"Noah...\"","Her blue eyes narrowed suspiciously.","\"...You’re not thinking something inappropriate, are you?\"","Noah looked at her innocently.","\"What do you mean, Mother?\" he asked, genuinely trying to appear confused.","She continued staring at him, unconvinced.","Noah immediately decided it was wiser to change the subject.","\"Oh, Brother,\" he said as he turned toward Nathan, \"when are you planning to get married? I think you’re old enough.\"","\"What?\"","Nathan frowned.","He had been peacefully enjoying his meal until Noah suddenly threw such an unexpected question at him.","\"Well, you know what I mean,\" Noah continued with a grin. \"You’re at the perfect age to bring Mother a wonderful daughter-in-law. She must get bored being the only woman in this manor.\"","\"Hey! I’m only twenty-six!\" Nathan protested. \"Why are you trying to marry me off so early?\"","\"Noah isn’t entirely wrong, Nathan,\" Catelyn said thoughtfully. \"If not marriage, then at least try dating someone.\"","She glanced at Noah for a brief moment before looking back at Nathan, as though she had suddenly remembered something important.","\"And the woman should be around your age...\"","She paused.","\"...Not older.\"","Noah’s lips twitched.","She was obviously referring to the joke he had made earlier about Morgana.","’Seriously... what’s wrong with Instructor Morgana? Noah complained inwardly. She’s only twenty-eight... or maybe twenty-nine. That’s still young. What’s so wrong if I wanted to marry her? She’s only ten years older.’","As far as he was concerned, there was absolutely nothing wrong with it.","\"Mother,\" Nathan said helplessly, \"I’ll date someone if I meet a woman who genuinely interests me.\"","Catelyn sighed softly.","\"I only hope you don’t remain single for the rest of your life.\"","Then Julian looked toward Noah.","\"By the way, Noah... I heard you’ve become quite close to Duke Sunweave’s daughter.\"","Noah frowned.","’What the hell...? Were they secretly keeping an eye on me? How did they even know something like that?’","Julian seemed to read the suspicion on his son’s face and chuckled.","\"Haha, don’t worry. I didn’t assign anyone to monitor your every move.\"","He calmly cut another piece of meat before continuing.","\"I learned it directly from Duke Sunweave himself. We were discussing official matters not long ago, and during our conversation he casually mentioned that his daughter had become rather close to you.\"","\"I... see.\"","’So Lyria must have mentioned me to her father... or perhaps Duke Sunweave had simply been keeping an eye on her. Considering she’ll become the future Saintess... that wouldn’t be surprising.’","\"I’ve met that girl before,\" Catelyn said with a gentle smile. \"She’s very sweet... and quite beautiful.\"","\"Cough...\"","Noah awkwardly cleared his throat.","\"Mother, I think we should leave that topic alone. I’m still young. There are many things I need to learn before thinking about relationships.\"","\"Very well.\"","She smiled knowingly before changing the subject.","\"Regardless, I’m truly happy that you managed to achieve second place.\"","Julian nodded in agreement before asking,","\"Tell me, Noah. Is there anything you want?\"","He paused briefly before adding,","\"Ah... although I suppose we still have to maintain the appearance of your exile before the other noble families. So I can’t lift the tag of exile from you.\"","\"I understand, Father.\"","Noah nodded.","\"There is something else I’d like to ask.\"","Julian looked at him.","\"Go ahead. You may ask for anything.\"","Noah straightened his posture before speaking respectfully.","\"Then... please train me while I’m here. I plan to spend my entire summer vacation training. Having your guidance would help me improve far more than practicing alone.\""]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: New Routine (1)","paragraphs":["The next morning,","Noah stood inside the Eldritch Household’s private training hall.","The hall was enormous, built to accommodate the family’s knights and guards. Rows of weapon racks lined the stone walls, filled with swords, spears, axes, shields, and bows. Several knights trained in the distance, their wooden weapons colliding rhythmically as instructors watched over them.","The ceiling rose several stories high, allowing enough space for large-scale combat training.","As one of the Four Great Ducal Houses of the empire, the Eldritch Family naturally possessed its own elite order of knights.","Noah wore simple training clothes—a plain black T-shirt, black trousers, and lightweight training shoes. His snow-white hair was tied into a short ponytail to keep it away from his eyes.","Standing opposite him was Julian Eldritch.","Unlike Noah, Julian wore a fitted white training shirt with black trousers. His posture remained perfectly straight, his expression calm and unreadable.","A wooden training sword rested loosely in his right hand.","Nathan stood several meters away with folded arms, silently observing the upcoming spar.","Father and son stood inside the marked sparring circle.","Noah held a genuine steel longsword.","Julian merely held a wooden sword.","\"I will personally guide your weapon training while you remain here,\" Julian said calmly. \"For magic, ask your mother. She is far more qualified than I am in that field.\"","\"Yes, Father.\"","Julian slowly raised his wooden sword.","\"Attack me with everything you know.\"","He paused before adding,","\"However, do not use your Ice Creation ability or any ice magic spells. You may reinforce your body with mana and use your swordsmanship. Any weapon art you know is acceptable.\"","Noah nodded.","\"...Understood.\"","Then he hesitated.","\"My newest sword art relies heavily on my ice affinity.\"","\"That is acceptable.\"","Julian nodded.","\"You may use the technique itself. Simply refrain from casting spells.\"","\"Understood.\"","Noah slowly lowered his center of gravity. His left foot slid backward.","His breathing steadied.","Mana surged from his core. It flowed through every mana channel before gathering around the steel blade.","A thin layer of mana coated the sword.","The edge immediately became sharper. Tiny crystalline particles gathered near the tip.","A single droplet of frost quietly formed.","[First Petal—Dewdrop Stance]","The surrounding temperature dropped noticeably. A faint frost-blue aura enveloped Noah’s body.","His silver eyes gradually turned into a pale icy blue.","Nathan raised an eyebrow. \"So that’s the Frost Lotus Blade Art he told me about...\"","Noah had told Nathan about what he had learned after leaving the house.","And of course, he simply told Nathan that he got the blade art from one of the dungeon he had visited. His brother also didn’t tried asking much in detail. No need to pry into unnecessary things. Afterall Nathan himself got more secrets.","While Julian’s expression showed slight interest.","\"Interesting.\"","Noah bent his knees.","Mana exploded beneath his feet.","Boom!","His figure vanished from his previous position. He rushed forward with astonishing speed.","The blade traced a graceful arc through the air. Tiny snowflakes drifted behind every movement.","The sword descended.","Clang!","Steel met wood.","No, it felt more like steel had collided with solid iron.","Noah’s arms trembled violently.","\"Urgh...\"","His teeth clenched.","The impact nearly forced the sword from his hands.","Julian hadn’t even moved his feet.","His wooden sword, protected by a thin coating of mana, had effortlessly blocked the strike.","Despite being made of wood, it hadn’t received the slightest scratch.","Frost rapidly crawled across Julian’s wooden sword.","Thin layers of ice attempted to spread.","Julian merely pushed a little more mana into the weapon.","Crack.","Every trace of frost shattered instantly.","\"So this is the freezing property of your sword art. Interesting, you were lucky to get such art.\"","Julian spoke calmly before lightly pushing Noah backward.","Noah slid several meters before stabilizing himself.","\"Again.\"","Noah inhaled deeply.","This time he decided to use the second form.","He slowly closed his eyes. The sounds inside the training hall gradually faded.","The clashing of weapons. The conversations of knights. Even his own breathing. Everything slowly disappeared.","There had been lingering sadness. There had been determination. There had been excitement at finally training under his father.","One after another those emotions quietly sank beneath a perfectly still surface.","Silence remained.","Only the sword existed. Only the path of the blade mattered.","Noah opened his eyes once more.","They no longer carried emotion.","Only absolute focus remained.","The air around him grew even colder than before.","Nathan immediately noticed the change.","\"...His presence changed.\"","Julian’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Seems like you are using another form of your weapon art.\"","His father didn’t tried to attack Noah. Firstly, he wanted to see what his son could do.","Noah disappeared.","Slash!","His movement looked unbelievably simple.","No unnecessary motion. No wasted strength. Only one perfectly refined horizontal slash.","For an instant a thin white line appeared within the air itself.","Shhhh—","An invisible blade of compressed freezing force flew toward Julian.","Julian calmly lifted his wooden sword.","Clang!","The invisible slash struck.","A sharp wave of frost exploded across the wooden blade.","The surrounding floor froze.","Crack!","Thin layers of ice rapidly spread across Julian’s weapon before breaking apart beneath overwhelming mana.","Noah immediately closed the distance.","Slash!","Slash!","Slash!","Each strike looked ordinary. Yet every swing carried invisible freezing force.","Julian blocked every attack effortlessly. He could feel the coldness that came out of each strike.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","The sound of wood and steel echoed throughout the hall.","Nathan watched silently.","\"...Father hasn’t taken a single step.\"","Meanwhile Noah had already launched over twenty attacks.","Every one of them had been blocked.","Finally Julian moved.","One simple swing.","Clang!","Noah’s sword was knocked aside.","Before Noah could recover.","Tap.","The wooden sword gently touched his chest.","\"If this were a real battle...\"","Julian looked at him calmly.","\"...you would already be dead.\"","For Julian it was too easy, but he was impressed by Noah.","Noah let out a long breath before lowering his sword.","\"I lost.\""]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: New Routine (2)","paragraphs":["\"I lost.\"","\"You were expected to.\"","Julian lowered his weapon.","\"There is nothing shameful about losing to someone with decades more experience.\"","He walked toward Noah.","\"However... There were many mistakes.\"","Noah immediately listened carefully.","\"First.\"","Julian raised one finger.","\"You relied too heavily on the freezing effect of your blade art rather than blade it self. What I mean is you rely more on ice than weapon. Your opponent won’t always fear the cold. If someone possesses stronger mana than you, they can simply shatter the frost, just as I did.\"","Noah nodded.","\"I understand.\"","\"Second.\"","\"Just now you focused entirely on offense. You never considered your own defense. Probably because of your ice creation ability, you rely on ice for defense that forms at your will too much. But in case of pure swordsmanship... you were too open\"","Julian tapped Noah’s shoulder with the wooden sword.","\"During your second petal, your concentration became absolute. That is both its greatest strength and its greatest weakness.\"","Noah frowned. But he understood what his father mean.","He was still learning the second form and haven’t reach 100% progression of it.","Julian nodded.","\"You became so focused on cutting me that you completely ignored my movements. If I had attacked your blind side... You wouldn’t have reacted.\"","Noah immediately realized it.","He had indeed entered a state where nothing existed except his own sword.","He hadn’t paid enough attention to Julian’s intentions.","\"Third.\"","Julian continued.","\"Your footwork. It’s good.\"","He pointed toward the floor.","\"But you attacked in straight lines. A predictable path. If I had wished, I could have redirected your momentum and broken your stance every single time.\"","Noah lowered his head slightly.","\"I’ll correct it.\"","Julian nodded approvingly.","\"The technique itself is excellent. I can see you might be more used to using your ice ability. I can see why its creator must be a master.\"","He paused before continuing.","\"But remember this, Noah. A sword or blade art never wins battles. The one who uses does.\"","Noah quietly engraved those words into his heart.","Julian turned around and walked back toward the center of the sparring circle.","\"Again.\"","\"This time...\"","\"Forget about defeating me. Focus only on correcting your mistakes.\"","A small smile appeared on Noah’s face.","\"...Yes, Father.\"","Without another word, he raised his sword once again.","The morning’s true training had only just begun.","---","Julian continued exchanging blows with Noah.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","The sharp sound of steel colliding against wood echoed throughout the training hall.","At first, Julian had only intended to evaluate his son’s current level.","After a few exchanges, however, he had already formed a clear assessment.","’His fundamentals are excellent.’","His stance was balanced. His grip on the sword was firm without being rigid. His breathing remained controlled, and his footwork was surprisingly clean.","Even his swordsmanship itself was far better than Julian had expected.","’His basics are solid. If someone had taught him, they laid an excellent foundation.’","Julian could immediately tell that Morgana had trained Noah well.","The problem did not lie in Noah’s swordsmanship.","It lay in how he fought. He relied too much on instinct and overwhelming offense.","Whenever he found an opening, he pursued it relentlessly, often exposing himself in return. He knew that this must be because of his ability. But he shouldn’t rely much one that.","He also became overly focused whenever he used the Second Petal, allowing his vision to narrow toward his target.","’He still lacks combat experience against opponents while fighting them with only weapons’","Without saying a word, Julian suddenly shifted from defense to offense.","Tap!","His wooden sword slipped past Noah’s guard and struck his shoulder.","\"Don’t watch my sword.\"","Julian spoke calmly.","\"Watch my entire body.\"","Before Noah could fully recover.","Thud!","Another strike landed lightly against his ribs.","\"You reacted too late.\"","That was cruel since Julian was just too fast for Noah.","Clang!","Noah hurriedly raised his blade to block the next attack.","Julian immediately changed the angle.","Smack!","The wooden sword struck Noah’s thigh.","Noah gritted his teeth but refused to retreat. Instead, he adjusted his stance and attacked once more.","Slash!","Julian parried effortlessly. Then counterattacked again.","Thud!","Another strike landed against Noah’s forearm. His grip loosened for a split second.","Noah immediately corrected his posture.","Again. And again.","Every mistake Julian pointed out disappeared after only one or two attempts.","That alone surprised him.","’...He’s learning too fast’","Most young swordsmen repeated the same mistake dozens of times before correcting it.","Noah rarely repeated it second or third time. Each exchange showed visible improvement. His defense became tighter. His footwork steadier. His attacks became less reckless.","Julian remained expressionless on the outside, yet inwardly he couldn’t hide his surprise.","’It seems Noah is an exceptionally fast learner. Far faster than I expected.’","Noah had spent most of his training using a spear rather than a sword.","Even when using a blade, he usually relied heavily on his Ice Creation ability.","Against few opponents, that approach had worked well.","But standing before Julian he had neither his ice spells nor his Ice Creation ability. He could only rely upon his body, his mana reinforcement, and his swordsmanship.","Oddly enough that limitation made Noah both excited and nervous. While his Adaptive learning ability made him learn things faster.","He wanted to perform well before his father. At the same time, he knew every mistake would be exposed immediately.","Sweat rolled down his forehead as they continued sparring.","His arms gradually grew heavier. His breathing became rougher. His muscles burned with exhaustion.","Yet every time Julian knocked him back...","Noah stood up again. Every time he was struck... He adjusted himself and attacked once more. He never complained. He never showed frustration. He simply learned. And continued swinging his sword.","Julian watched him quietly. A faint smile almost appeared on his face before disappearing just as quickly.","’Good...This is the determination I wanted to see.’","His son was no longer the spoiled young noble who had once avoided hardship. Standing before him now was a young swordsman willing to endure pain in order to grow stronger.","Julian truly felt proud of Noah.","---","\"So... are you ready to study now?\"","\"...Yes.\"","Noah took a moment before answering.","Currently, he was sitting inside the grand library of the Eldritch Manor.","Seated beside him at a large wooden table was his mother.","Several thick books were neatly stacked in front of her, each one dedicated exclusively to the study of ice magic.","\"M-Mother...\" Noah said with a helpless smile. \"I’m already learning so much at the academy. I don’t think I really need to—\"","Catelyn gently closed one of the books and looked at him with a calm smile.","\"These aren’t ordinary textbooks.\"","She lightly tapped the stack before her.","\"Every one of these books is dedicated to ice magic. Since your affinity is ice as well, there’s no better time for you to study them.\"","Then she tilted her head slightly.","\"...Or are you already tired?\"","It was already late afternoon.","Noah had spent the entire morning and early afternoon training under Julian’s strict guidance before sharing lunch with his family.","Now, instead of resting he found himself sitting in the library, about to begin another lesson.","He let out a quiet sigh before shaking his head.","\"No.\"","He still had a long way to go. If he wanted to survive the future. He couldn’t afford to slack off.","Noah straightened his posture and looked at his mother with determination.","\"Alright, Mother. I’m ready.\"","---","[A/N: Sorry about these last two Chapters. I just wanted to show that the MC trains hard and doesn’t only flirt around!]"]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: New Mission","paragraphs":["It was the fifth month of the year 2048.","More than fifteen days had passed since Noah had returned to the Eldritch Manor.","Almost all of his time had been devoted to training.","Not every day did Julian have time to personally train him. As the Duke of Eldritch, he carried countless responsibilities, and most of his days were occupied with official duties and meetings.","Whenever Julian was unavailable, Nathan took his place.","His elder brother was currently at the Mythril Core (High) realm.","He was far stronger than Noah.","Every morning, the two brothers sparred and trained together for several hours. Nathan would patiently correct Noah’s mistakes before leaving the training hall to attend to his own responsibilities.","As the future heir of the Eldritch Household, Nathan had plenty of work waiting for him.","After training, Noah would return to his room, freshen up, and relax for a while.","Sometimes he watched television. Sometimes he played games on his phone.","Then came lunch with his family.","Later in the afternoon, he would head to the library, where Catelyn patiently taught him the theory behind ice magic, mana control, spell construction, and advanced magical principles until evening.","His schedule had become almost identical every single day.","A peaceful routine. And before he realized it. He had grown accustomed to it.","\"Damn...\"","Noah leaned comfortably against the chair on one of the manor’s spacious balconies.","\"This kind of life is incredibly peaceful.\"","The evening breeze gently brushed past him.","The sky had already begun turning shades of orange and crimson as the sun slowly descended toward the horizon.","He had just finished another lesson with his mother.","A warm cup of coffee rested in his hand.","Whether it was morning or evening, Noah always enjoyed drinking either coffee or tea.","It had quietly become one of his favorite habits.","Resting comfortably on his lap was Nancy.","The black-furred cat had curled herself into a small ball, lazily enjoying the gentle warmth.","Noah absentmindedly stroked her silky fur with his free hand.","A relaxed smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"I wish life could just continue like this.\"","He looked toward the sunset stretching across the distant mountains.","\"Wake up, Eat something light...Train until I become stronger...Eat again... Watch TV or play games for a while...Study magic...Eat dinner...Scroll through my phone while petting a cute cat...And then sleep.\"","He chuckled softly.","\"It really isn’t a bad life.\"","After a brief silence, his smile gradually faded.","\"It would’ve been even better if there weren’t demons, villains, and monsters constantly trying to destroy the world.\"","His gaze drifted toward the distant sky.","\"And especially...it’s much better if there isn’t a villain who’s willing to sacrifice the entire world just to save his lover.\"","He sighed.","\"I seriously have no desire to die just because someone else wants to save the person they love.\"","He took another sip of his coffee before continuing.","\"In that situation...I’m definitely on the heroes’ side. At least if the heroes save the world...I will be safe.\"","Noah smiled helplessly before looking down at Nancy.","\"Don’t you think so, Nancy?\"","\"Meow~\"","The little cat lazily replied without even opening her eyes.","Noah laughed quietly.","\"You know... I used to like villains much more than heroes.\"","He gently scratched beneath Nancy’s chin.","\"But after actually living in a world like this and facing those dangers...I honestly hope people stay kind. I hope heroes continue protecting everyone. Including me.\"","His thoughts naturally drifted toward Damien. The young man was destined to become humanity’s greatest hero.","The one who would stand against the greatest darkness this world had ever known.","’I should support Damien as much as I can... He’s the future hero, after all.’","BEEP!","BEEP!","The ringtone suddenly echoed from inside his pocket.","Noah frowned.","\"Hm? Who’s calling me?\"","He pulled his phone out.","\"Lyria? Or maybe Arisha?\"","He wondered aloud.","The moment his eyes landed on the screen...","His expression immediately darkened.","\"...\"","The caller’s name was displayed in large letters.","Damien Ashworth.","Noah’s lips twitched.","\"...Damien?\"","He stared at the screen with obvious dissatisfaction.","\"Why is that devil calling me?\"","Just a moment ago, he had been thinking about Damien.","And now the man himself had called.","Noah let out a helpless sigh.","\"...Talk about summoning the devil.\"","Noah let out a quiet sigh before accepting the call.","He raised the phone to his ear.","\"What is it?\"","A cheerful laugh immediately came from the other side.","\"Haha! Noah! How are you doing?","\"I’m doing well.\" Noah leaned back against his chair and took another sip of his coffee. \"What about you?\"","\"I’m doing great, man.\"","\"...\"","A brief silence followed.","\"So...\"","Noah spoke flatly.","\"...why did you call me?\"","\"Can’t I call my own friend?\" Damien complained dramatically. \"I miss you.\"","Noah clicked his tongue.","\"Tch. Stop talking like a gay.\"","\"Get to the point.\"","There was another brief silence.","\"...Fuck you.\"","Damien sounded utterly offended.","\"I’m not gay!\"","\"Then start talking.\"","Damien let out a long sigh.","\"...Alright. Listen carefully.\"","\"I’m listening.\"","\"So at the beginning of this month, Master brought me here.\"","Noah frowned.","\"...here?\"","He raised an eyebrow.","\"Do you honestly think I know where you are? At least explain it properly.\"","\"Oh, right.\"","Damien laughed awkwardly.","\"I’m currently staying in a city called Everhold. It’s inside the Duchy of Thornveil.\"","Noah became silent for a moment.","’Everhold...Thornveil...’","He knew that place.","It was the territory where Ophelia’s family ruled.","\"So? What about it?\"","\"I came here with Master for training.\"","\"Good for you.\"","Damien continued excitedly.","\"And now she’s going to throw me—\"","He immediately corrected himself.","\"...I mean, she wants me to enter a labyrinth.\"","Noah frowned.","\"A labyrinth? Shouldn’t something like that already be under the control of either the Adventurers’ Guild or the Thornveil Ducal Family?\"","\"Hehe.\"","Damien chuckled proudly.","\"That’s the interesting part. It wasn’t discovered by anyone. I found it.\"","Noah blinked.","\"...You found a labyrinth?\"","\"Yeah. My master threw me into a forest for survival training. And while wandering around... I accidentally discovered its entrance. So we decided not to report it immediately.\"","\"Master is currently inspecting the entire labyrinth herself. She’s checking whether it’s safe enough for me. If there are monsters beyond what I can handle... Or any hidden dangers... She’ll deal with them first.\"","\"I see...\"","Noah nodded slightly.","That certainly sounded like something Morgana would do.","She was strict... But she never threw Damien into truly hopeless situations.","Then Noah asked,","\"...So why exactly are you telling me all of this?\"","Damien laughed.","\"Because I wanted to invite you. You remember when we explored that dungeon together? And we’ve both trained under Master Morgana before. It’ll be much better if we explore the labyrinth together.\"","\"We can train...Fight stronger monsters... And honestly... I think it’ll be much safer if you’re with me.\"","Noah didn’t answer immediately.","He quietly stared at the evening sky beyond the balcony.","’A newly discovered labyrinth...Knowing Damien’s protagonist luck... There’s definitely something valuable hidden inside. Which also means... There’s definitely something dangerous hidden inside.’","He rubbed his forehead.","’The system will reward me if I accompany him and clear the labyrinth, since it might be one of the act of game.’","Several thoughts crossed his mind. After remaining silent for a few moments.","Noah finally nodded to himself.","Then he calmly spoke into the phone.","\"I don’t want to come.\"","Damien’s voice instantly turned cheerful.","\"Great! Then come as fast as you can—\"","He suddenly paused.","\"...Wait. Did you just refuse?\"","His tone rose in disbelief.","\"Why don’t you want to come?\"","Noah let out a helpless sigh before replying.","\"You do remember what happened the last time we entered a dungeon together, don’t you? We encountered something completely unknown. I have no desire to experience something like that again.\"","Silence followed on Damien’s side.","\"Pfft... Hahahaha!\"","Loud laughter echoed through the phone.","\"Oh, Noah... damn you! I never thought you were such a coward!\"","A vein throbbed on Noah’s forehead.","But he remained cool. \"I am not a coward. I am just being careful.\" he said calmly.","\"Excuses.\"","Damien clicked his tongue dramatically.","\"I thought you wanted to become stronger. I thought you wanted to face danger and grow through it.\"","He chuckled again.","\"But I guess I was wrong. You are just a coward like others.\"","Noah slowly closed his eyes.","’Calm down...Don’t fall for it...He is obviously trying to provoke me into agreeing.’","He took a slow breath before answering in an indifferent voice.","\"If calling me a coward makes you happy, then go ahead.\"","\"Oh, I definitely will.\"","Damien sounded far too pleased.","\"I’ll make sure to tell Master Morgana that the great Noah Eldritch got scared of a little labyrinth.\"","He burst into another fit of laughter.","\"Hahaha!\"","That was the final straw.","Noah abruptly stood up from his chair.","\"Damn you, bastard!\" he shouted into the phone. \"Do you seriously think you can force me into coming?\"","\"Never!\"","---","Later that night...","Noah stood inside his bedroom with an open travel bag resting on the bed. One by one, he folded his clothes and packed everything he would need for the journey.","His sword lay beside the bag, along with several mana recovery potions and other necessities.","Nancy sat comfortably on the bed, lazily watching him move around the room with half-open golden eyes.","Noah stuffed another set of clothes into the bag before letting out a long, defeated sigh.","\"Dammit... In the end, I still agreed.\"","He rubbed his forehead in frustration.","He zipped the bag shut before placing it beside the bed.","After standing silently for a moment, his expression gradually became more serious.","\"...Well, I had to go eventually. If Damien discovered a labyrinth by chance, there was a good possibility that something valuable existed inside.\"","His eyes narrowed thoughtfully.","\"I needed to learn everything I possibly could for the future. There were still too many unknowns in this world. And the stronger I became now...the higher my chances of surviving later. Surviving while running from danger is no worth. It’s better to die earlier rather than running away from them.\"","Noah just wanted to spend his vacation peacefully. But it appears, his luck was affected by Damien a long time ago.","He glanced toward the packed bag before letting out another sigh.","\"Though one thing I do know, it would turn into another disaster.\""]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Labyrinth [1]","paragraphs":["The next morning, Noah was fully prepared for his new journey.","He stood inside the study, wearing comfortable travel clothes with a backpack slung over one shoulder. For looking good and then put it inside storage ring once he left the house.","His mother, Catelyn, looked him over.","\"Where are you going?\" she asked.","\"I am going to meet a friend,\" Noah replied calmly. \"He wanted to explore a labyrinth together.\"","\"What?\"","Catelyn frowned immediately.","\"Out of nowhere?\"","She folded her arms across her chest before firing one question after another.","\"Who is this friend? How many of you are going? Where is this labyrinth? Which city is it located in?\"","Before Noah could answer, Julian looked up from the documents on his desk.","\"Catelyn,\" he said calmly, \"stop asking so many questions.\"","He leaned back in his chair.","\"If Noah wishes to go, then let him.\"","The three of them were currently inside the Duke’s study.","Catelyn let out a small sigh.","\"I am not trying to stop him.\"","She glanced at Noah before continuing in a gentler voice.","\"I simply want to know exactly where he is going. What if something happens to him? At the very least, we should know where to find him.\"","Hearing that, Noah patiently explained everything.","He told her that he would be meeting Damien Ashworth in Everhold City, located within the Thornveil Duchy. He also explained that they would be exploring a newly discovered labyrinth together and that Instructor Morgana would personally inspect it beforehand to ensure it was safe enough for them.","For a brief moment, Catelyn narrowed her eyes after hearing Morgana’s name.","\"...I see.\"","She slowly nodded before pushing the money pouch toward Noah.","\"Very well. You may have this.\"","Then she looked directly into his eyes.","\"And don’t bother your Instructor Morgana too much.\"","For some reason, she placed unusual emphasis on Morgana’s name.","Noah’s lips twitched slightly.","He had absolutely no intention of explaining anything.","Right now, all he wanted was to leave before another misunderstanding occurred.","\"As you say, Mother,\" he replied obediently.","Catelyn smiled faintly before stepping closer and wrapping him in a brief, gentle embrace.","\"And lastly...Take care of yourself. Stay safe.\"","Noah returned the hug before nodding.","\"I will.\"","Julian then spoke from behind his desk.","\"You are heading to Everhold, the capital city of the Thornveil Duchy. It is also where the Duke’s family resides.\"","His expression remained calm and dignified.","\"You should not encounter any problems there.\"","He paused briefly before adding,","\"However... try your best not to cross paths with your former fiancée. The Thornveil family does not hate you personally, but avoiding unnecessary encounters would still be the wiser choice.\"","Noah nodded respectfully.","\"I understand, Father.\"","He bowed to both of his parents.","\"I will take my leave.\"","Just before leaving, he looked toward his mother.","\"Mother, could you please take care of Nancy while I am gone?\"","Catelyn smiled gently.","\"Leave her to me. You may travel without worrying.\"","Satisfied, Noah gave one final nod before turning around and leaving the study.","Not long afterward...","Noah stepped through a teleportation gate.","A bright flash of light engulfed him for an instant before the scenery around him completely changed.","He slowly opened his eyes.","\"Not bad.\"","A faint smile appeared on his face.","Using the teleportation network had allowed him to travel across the Empire in only a few moments.","\"It’s good to be rich.\"","He muttered those words with satisfaction.","The Thornveil Duchy was located in the southern region of the Empire.","Unlike the colder northern lands ruled by the Eldritch family, the climate here was considerably warmer.","Noah looked around the bustling streets.","\"Tch... It’s still not as beautiful as my duchy.\"","Everhold was undoubtedly prosperous.","Wide roads stretched through the city, modern vehicles moved in orderly traffic, and elegant commercial buildings lined both sides of the streets. People hurried about their daily lives, filling the city with energy.","Yet despite all its wealth and development, Noah failed to find anything particularly unique about it.","To him, it simply resembled another modern metropolitan city.","Nothing more.","He left the teleportation station and boarded a public bus that traveled toward the outskirts of the city.","Nearly forty minutes later, he stepped off at the final stop near the edge of the city. He left the city and came to edge of a vast forest.","Towering trees stretched endlessly before him, while distant mountain ranges rose against the horizon.","A cool breeze drifted through the wilderness.","\"The world really is enormous.\"","He quietly observed his surroundings.","\"Almost every major city seems to be surrounded by forests and mountains. I suppose that’s actually a good thing.\"","After all, monsters and magical beasts naturally inhabited such environments, making them ideal locations for adventurers, training grounds, and valuable resource gathering.","Noah glanced around.","\"So... Where is that protagonist bastard?\"","Damien had already explained how to reach this location.","Now all Noah had to do was wait.","A few moments later—","\"Hey, Noah!!\"","A familiar voice echoed from behind him.","Noah turned around.","Sure enough, Damien emerged from between the trees with his usual carefree grin plastered across his face, casually walking out of the forest as if he had been waiting there all along.","Damien walked toward Noah with his usual carefree grin.","The moment he reached him, he extended his hand.","Noah accepted it without hesitation, and the two shook hands firmly.","\"How have you been, Noah?\" Damien asked with a cheerful smile. \"It’s good to see that you’ve fully recovered.\"","Unlike his academy uniform, Damien wore simple travel clothes beneath a set of light leather armor reinforced with metal plates around the shoulders and chest. A sword hung comfortably at his waist, while a travel backpack rested behind him.","He looked completely prepared for an expedition.","Noah smiled back.","\"I have been doing well.\"","He returned the handshake before adding,","\"And I am glad to see you again too.\"","Damien laughed.","\"Good.\"","He turned toward the forest.","\"Come on. Master is waiting for us.\"","The two of them began walking deeper into the forest together.","As they traveled along the narrow path between towering trees, Damien casually started talking about the past two weeks.","\"I swear, training here all alone was torture.\"","He sighed dramatically.","\"Master didn’t let me slack off even for a single day. Morning training. Afternoon training. Evening training. I seriously thought I was going to die.\"","Noah chuckled quietly.","\"That does sound like Instructor Morgana.\"","After listening for a while, he asked,","\"Why did Instructor Morgana choose this place in the first place?\"","Damien shrugged.","\"She told me there were several monster species living around this region that I had never fought before. She wanted me to gain experience against unfamiliar geography.\"","He scratched the back of his head before continuing.","\"Oh... and she also mentioned that she had some business with the Duke of Thornveil. That was the main reason.\""]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Labyrinth [2]","paragraphs":["Noah simply nodded.","\"I see.\"","He did not ask any further questions. Though he was curious at what Morgana had to talk with duke Thornveil’s family.","He knew that Morgana was also from a count’s family.","’So they might have some deals. If I am not wrong she’s going to be countess of her family in future.’","The two continued walking through the forest.","Unlike the northern forests of the Eldritch Duchy, many of the trees here had already shed their leaves. Countless bare branches stretched toward the sky, creating a strange yet beautiful landscape.","Dry leaves crunched beneath their boots with every step.","Occasionally, birds flew overhead while the distant cries of magical beasts echoed from deeper within the mountains.","The scenery remained peaceful.","They continued walking for nearly an hour.","Eventually, Noah frowned slightly.","\"...How much farther?\"","Damien looked ahead before grinning.","\"We’re close. Let’s run from here.\"","Without waiting for a reply, Damien immediately accelerated.","Mana surged through his body as he shot forward like an arrow.","\"Tch...\"","Noah clicked his tongue before wrapping mana around his legs as well.","His body became noticeably lighter.","The two sprinted across the forest at incredible speed.","Trees blurred past them as they leaped over rocks, crossed narrow streams, and dashed through winding paths without slowing down.","Nearly thirty minutes later. They finally arrived at the base of a small mountain.","Standing there calmly with her arms folded was Morgana.","She had already changed into practical combat attire instead of her usual outfit. Light armor covered her upper body.","The moment Noah saw her, he walked forward respectfully.","\"Instructor Morgana.\"","He gave a polite bow along with a small smile.","\"It is good to see you again.\"","Morgana gave him a brief nod.","\"It is good to see that you have fully recovered.\"","She mostly mean mentally.","Her gaze shifted between the two young men.","\"So...Are both of you ready?\"","\"Yes,\" Noah answered immediately.","Damien nodded as well.","\"We’re ready, Master.\"","Noah hesitated for a moment before asking,","\"Instructor... Are you certain there isn’t any real danger inside?\"","Morgana calmly replied,","\"There shouldn’t be. I have already explored most of the labyrinth myself.\"","She then glanced at Damien.","\"I also gave Damien an emergency communication device. If anything unexpected happens, he only needs to activate it. I will receive the signal immediately and come to rescue both of you.\"","Hearing those words, Noah finally felt much more at ease.","\"That’s reassuring.\"","He let out a quiet breath.","Without wasting any more time, Noah reached into his storage ring.","A flash of light appeared.","The next moment, a set of light combat armor materialized in his hands.","He quickly equipped the armor over his clothes before adjusting the straps securely around his shoulders and waist.","After that, another flash emerged from the storage ring.","His sword appeared in his right hand.","Noah gripped the hilt firmly before looking toward Morgana with determined eyes.","\"I am ready.\"","---","Damien walked forward, and Noah quietly followed behind him.","Instead of climbing the mountain, Damien led him toward a rugged section near its base where countless jagged rocks and massive boulders were scattered across the ground.","To an ordinary person, it appeared to be nothing more than a natural rock formation.","However, after weaving through several enormous boulders, Damien suddenly stopped.","Hidden behind one of the largest rocks was a narrow opening barely wide enough for a single person to pass through.","If someone did not know where to look, they would never notice it.","\"So this is the entrance,\" Noah muttered.","Damien nodded with a grin.","\"Yep.\"","Without another word, he stepped inside.","Noah followed him closely.","The passage was surprisingly narrow and completely engulfed in darkness.","Only the sound of their footsteps echoed through the confined tunnel.","After walking several meters, Damien raised his right hand.","A small sphere of white light materialized above his palm, illuminating the rocky passage ahead.","The magical light chased away the darkness, allowing both of them to continue deeper underground.","The tunnel gradually widened.","Several minutes later, they reached the end.","A massive stone gate stood before them.","Ancient symbols were carved across its weathered surface, while thick layers of dust hinted that it had remained untouched for countless years.","\"So this is the labyrinth...\" Noah murmured softly.","Damien placed both hands against the heavy stone door.","\"Help me a little.\"","Noah stepped forward and pushed as well.","Rumble...","The enormous gate slowly creaked open, releasing a deep rumbling sound that echoed throughout the underground passage.","Dust drifted through the air as the ancient entrance revealed itself.","Damien walked through first.","Noah immediately followed.","The instant he crossed the threshold, he felt a strange sensation wash over his entire body.","It lasted for only a brief moment.","It was almost as though he had passed through an invisible membrane or perhaps a portal.","He instinctively looked behind him.","The entrance appeared exactly the same.","’Was that... my imagination? Or is this one of those labyrinth who are located in different small dimension.’ Noah wondered.","He could not tell. Before he had time to think further.","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","One after another, the mana torches mounted along the stone walls suddenly ignited with pale blue flames.","The corridor brightened instantly.","The entire passage came into view.","Its walls, floor, and ceiling were all constructed from neatly arranged gray stone bricks. The craftsmanship looked ancient, yet every brick remained perfectly intact despite the countless years that had passed.","The long corridor stretched far into the distance, disappearing into darkness once again.","Damien smiled confidently.","\"Let’s go.\"","Without hesitation, he began walking deeper into the labyrinth.","After taking one last glance at the ancient entrance behind him, Noah tightened his grip on his sword and silently followed.","Though Labyrinth didn’t have much monster like those in dungeon.","But it’s more focus on traps and maize like progression and exploration.","Whatever danger lay ahead, Noah was ready to face it.","---","[A/N: Well it was supposed to be a single Chapter. But as my habit I yap a lot and write to huge chap. So decided to spilt them into two! kekeke!!"]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Labyrinth [3]","paragraphs":["\"So... this is a Labyrinth...\"","Noah’s voice dropped to a whisper as he slowly surveyed his surroundings.","It was the first labyrinth he had entered since arriving in this world. The atmosphere felt completely different from a dungeon. The air was unnaturally cool.","Not cold enough to sting the skin, yet chilly enough to send a faint shiver down his spine. There was no breeze. No dripping water. No distant rumble.","Only an oppressive silence that seemed to press against their ears. It felt as though the labyrinth itself was holding its breath.","The only sound came from their footsteps.","Click.","Click.","Click.","Each step echoed throughout the endless corridors before returning a moment later from strange directions that made little sense.","Damien frowned.","\"...Did that echo come from behind us?\"","Noah stopped walking. Both of them remained perfectly still, listening carefully.","Silence.","Nothing answered them.","\"...Probably,\" Noah muttered.","Neither of them sounded convinced.","They continued forward until the narrow corridor suddenly opened into a massive circular chamber.","Six identical passageways branched out in different directions.","Each entrance was flanked by an ancient stone pillar covered in faded carvings whose meanings had long been forgotten.","Damien scratched the back of his head.","\"So...\"","\"We have to choose one.\"","Noah glanced at the six identical paths.","\"Any idea which one?\"","\"No.\"","Damien answered without hesitation.","The two exchanged amused looks.","\"I was hoping you’d have some brilliant plan,\" Damien said with disappointment.","\"I was hoping you’d pretend to have one.\"","A faint chuckle escaped both of them.","For a brief moment, the tense atmosphere eased.","’How exactly did Instructor Morgana inspect this entire labyrinth?’","Noah wondered inwardly. He could not imagine mapping such a place alone.","After looking around once more, he asked,","\"Anyway... which path should we take?\"","Truthfully, Noah had already made up his mind.","If anyone possessed absurd luck, it was the protagonist standing beside him.","Damien’s intuition had a habit of leading him toward opportunities. Or disasters. Sometimes both. Damien folded his arms and stared at the six corridors. He remained completely silent.","One minute passed.","Then another. Finally, he pointed toward the third passage.","\"We’re taking the third route.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Why?\"","Damien shrugged casually.","\"Don’t ask. It’s just my intuition.\"","A small smile appeared on Noah’s face.","’I’ll trust the protagonist’s intuition.’","\"Fine.\"","\"Let’s go.\"","Without another word, the two entered the third passageway.","The corridor stretched endlessly before them.","The walls remained unchanged, built entirely from ancient gray stone bricks illuminated by flickering mana torches.","For several minutes, nothing happened.","The only sound was their steady footsteps.","Then—","Scrape...","The noise echoed from somewhere ahead.","Stone grinding against stone.","It was slow, heavy and deliberate.","Both young men immediately stopped.","Their relaxed expressions disappeared.","Scrape...","The sound came again.","Closer this time.","Then another.","From the darkness ahead, a massive figure slowly emerged.","At first glance, it looked like part of the wall itself.","Then it moved.","The creature stood nearly three meters tall.","Its entire body had been carved from cracked gray stone.","Thick moss covered its broad shoulders, while glowing blue flames burned within the hollow sockets where eyes should have been.","Its enormous fists scraped across the ground as it advanced, carving deep grooves into the ancient stone floor.","A Forgotten Guardian. The giant slowly lifted its head. The blue flames within its eyes burned brighter.","For a single heartbeat neither side moved.","BOOM!","The guardian took one thunderous step forward. The entire path trembled violently.","Dust drifted from the ceiling. The labyrinth had finally acknowledged its newest visitors.","A grin spread across Damien’s face.","\"There it is.\"","Noah slowly drew his sword. \"Well, brother... Get ready.\"","Mana surged from Noah’s core.","It flowed rapidly through every part of his body, strengthening his muscles and sharpening his senses.","The mana then gathered around the blade of his sword, forming an incredibly thin layer of ice along its edge.","The weapon gleamed with a faint frost-blue light.","At the same time, golden mana erupted around Damien’s body.","His aura grew noticeably heavier.","\"Let’s destroy it!\"","Without waiting another second, Damien exploded forward.","Boom!","The stone floor cracked beneath his feet as he launched himself straight toward the guardian.","Noah followed immediately behind him.","The Forgotten Guardian raised its enormous stone fist.","Damien met it head-on.","CLANG!","His sword collided against the giant’s rocky arm, releasing a deafening metallic sound.","Although the guardian possessed tremendous physical strength, Damien had already reached the Condensed Core (Low) realm.","His raw power was more than enough to contend with it directly.","The guardian’s massive body staggered backward by half a step.","\"Your turn!\"","Damien shouted.","Noah immediately extended his free hand.","Ice Creation, his ability kicked in.","Mana erupted from beneath the guardian’s feet.","Crack!","Crack!","Thick layers of ice burst upward from the stone floor, rapidly wrapping around both of the giant’s legs.","Within seconds, its lower body had been completely frozen in place. The Forgotten Guardian roared silently as it struggled to move.","The ice cracked violently under its overwhelming strength.","But it bought them exactly what they needed.","Damien smiled.","\"Perfect!\"","Golden mana gathered around his sword.","He leaped high into the air before bringing his weapon crashing down with tremendous force. His blade shone so brightly that it made the darkness ran away from the passage.","[Heavenly Sacred Radiance]","He used the first form of the sword art, but not with it’s full power.","BOOM!","The golden blade struck the guardian’s shoulder, creating a deep crack across its stone body. Fragments of rock scattered everywhere. The guardian swung its enormous arm toward Damien.","Noah moved instantly. He dashed behind the creature.","His sword flashed.","Slash!","A clean cut appeared behind one of its knees.","Frost spread rapidly from the wound, further weakening the already frozen joint.","The guardian lost its balance.","Its massive body tilted forward.","\"Now!\"","Damien understood immediately.","Gathering all his strength, he lunged once more.","Golden mana exploded around him.","Clang!","His sword pierced straight through the guardian’s cracked chest.","For a brief moment, everything became still.","CRACK!","Countless fractures spread across the guardian’s entire body.","Blue light leaked from every crack.","A second later—","BOOM!!","The Forgotten Guardian shattered into hundreds of stone fragments that scattered across the chamber floor.","Silence returned.","The only sounds remaining were the small pieces of stone rolling across the ground.","Damien lowered his sword onto his shoulder.","\"That was easier than I expected.\"","Noah exhaled slowly before returning his sword to his side.","\"It wasn’t particularly strong.\"","The two exchanged satisfied smiles. If every guardian inside the labyrinth was around this level...","Their exploration had just become far more promising.","Noah felt more confident about there incoming journey.","’Maybe, this is just a normal labyrinth.’ He thought for a second before dismissing it. Wherever this protagonist Damien was present, danger would always followed there."]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: Labyrinth [4]","paragraphs":["After defeating the Forgotten Guardian, the two continued deeper into the labyrinth.","The ancient corridor stretched onward, illuminated by rows of pale blue mana torches fixed to the stone walls. Aside from the occasional sound of their footsteps, the labyrinth remained eerily silent.","Neither of them lowered their guard.","Several minutes later, the corridor widened once again. Another intersection appeared before them. Just like before, four separate passageways branched off in different directions.","Noah looked from one tunnel to another before letting out a helpless sigh. \"Damn...This really does feel like a maze.\" Damien said with irritation.","Every corridor looked exactly the same.","\"Well, because it is one.\"","The walls. The floor. Even the torches. There wasn’t a single landmark that could help distinguish one path from another.","Damien folded his arms and stared at the four routes.","\"Hmm...\"","After only a few seconds, he pointed toward the second passage.","\"We’re taking this one.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Your intuition again?\"","Damien grinned proudly.","\"Exactly.\"","Noah simply shrugged.","\"I’ll trust it.\"","The two walked toward the second passage.","Damien stepped forward first.","The moment his foot landed inside—","Click.","A faint mechanical sound echoed beneath him.","\"Huh?\"","Damien instinctively looked down.","The stone beneath his feet suddenly split apart.","Rumble!","The floor collapsed without warning.","Damien’s eyes widened.","\"Oh, shi—!\"","He completely lost his balance and began falling into the darkness below.","Fortunately, Noah reacted instantly. He lunged forward and grabbed Damien’s wrist just before he disappeared into the pit.","His boots dug into the stone floor as he braced himself against the sudden weight.","\"Got you.\"","Damien looked up in surprise. For a brief moment, relief washed across his face.","Noah stood firmly at the edge of the pit while holding onto him with one hand.","A grin slowly spread across his face.","He opened his mouth, ready to say,","\"Saved you, brother—\"","Before he could finish—","Click!","Another mechanism activated.","Noah’s expression instantly changed.","\"Dammit!\"","From hidden openings within both walls.","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Dozens of arrows shot toward them at terrifying speed.","Each arrow shimmered with mana, making them far deadlier than ordinary projectiles.","There was no time to dodge. Noah immediately yanked Damien upward with all his strength.","At the same time, he thrust his free hand forward.","Mana erupted from his core.","Crack!","A massive wall of solid ice burst from the ground directly in front of them.","The arrows struck it a heartbeat later.","Bang!","Bang!","Bang!","The mana-coated arrows slammed into the ice with tremendous force.","Cracks spread rapidly across its surface.","Some arrows even embedded themselves halfway through the wall.","The barrage continued for several seconds before finally coming to an end.","Silence returned.","The ice wall was covered in countless fractures, barely holding together.","Noah slowly let out the breath he had been holding.","\"...That was close.\"","Damien climbed fully onto solid ground before looking at the shattered trap beneath them.","Then he turned toward Noah with an awkward smile.","\"Heh... I owe you one.\"","Noah rolled his eyes.","\"You definitely do.\"","Damien scratched the back of his head before laughing.","\"Thanks, brother. If you hadn’t reacted that quickly, I’d probably still be at the bottom of that pit.\"","Noah glanced toward the dark hole before muttering,","\"And I almost got turned into a porcupine trying to save you.\"","Damien laughed even harder.","\"Well at least we’re both still alive... hehe what am I even saying. This level of danger cannot kill us.\"","Noah sighed helplessly.","\"Let’s be more careful from now on. The labyrinths have more traps and ability to confused a person. And less monsters.\"","\"Yes. Let’s go to fourth passage.\"","Damien started walking again as though nothing had happened.","Noah stared at him in disbelief.","The guy hadn’t even taken a minute to think before choosing another path.","\"...Unbelievable.\"","He let out a helpless sigh and followed after him.","Not that he had a better method of choosing the correct route.","This time, however, they proceeded far more cautiously.","Before taking a single step into the corridor, Noah formed a solid ball of ice in his palm.","\"Ice Creation.\"","He tossed it forward.","The ice sphere bounced across the stone floor several times.","Thud.","Thud.","Thud.","Nothing happened.","No hidden mechanisms activated.","No arrows flew from the walls.","No floor collapsed beneath it.","\"It looks safe,\" Noah said.","Damien nodded.","\"Let’s move.\"","The two cautiously advanced through the passage.","Click.","Click.","Only their footsteps echoed through the silent corridor.","After walking for a while, Damien suddenly broke the silence.","\"Noah.\"","\"Hm?\"","Noah turned his head.","\"What is it?\"","Damien hesitated for a moment before asking, \"...Do you still love Ophelia?\"","Noah almost stumbled.","\"The hell? Where did that come from?\"","Damien scratched the back of his head awkwardly.","\"Well... I didn’t know anything about what happened before in detail. But after everything that happened during the semester, I asked Master Morgana. She told me the whole story.\"","He looked at Noah with a sympathetic expression.","\"So... you really loved her.\"","He paused briefly.","\"I was just wondering if you still felt the same.\"","Since he had been staying within the Thornveil Duchy for the past week, hearing Ophelia’s name from local people had naturally reminded him of Noah.","Noah remained silent for a few seconds.","Then he calmly shook his head.","\"No. I don’t. My heart beats for someone else now.\"","Damien blinked in surprise.","He had genuinely felt sorry for Noah after learning the truth behind his exile. He had assumed Noah was still carrying those feelings. And tries to tease Arisha and Lyria just for fun.","Apparently...","He had been completely wrong.","\"So you’ve already moved on?\"","\"Yes.\"","Damien’s curiosity immediately took over. A mischievous grin spread across his face.","\"So... Who is she?\"","He leaned closer.","\"Is it Lyria? Or Arisha?\"","Those were the only two girls Damien had ever seen Noah spending time with.","\"No.\"","Noah answered immediately.","\"Neither of them.\"","Damien looked even more surprised.","\"Really? Then who? Come on, tell me! I might even help you.\"","A faint smirk appeared on Noah’s face.","\"Sure. I think you’re exactly the right person to ask for help.\"","Damien puffed out his chest proudly.","\"See? I knew it. So who is she?\"","Noah looked straight at him before replying with a perfectly serious expression.","\"Instructor Morgana.\"","Damien’s smile froze.","\"...What?\"","His eyes widened.","Before he could even process those words.","THUD!","The entire corridor shook violently.","Both young men immediately turned toward the source of the sound. From the darkness ahead...","A massive stone figure slowly emerged.","Its body was covered in cracks, thick moss clung to its shoulders, and blue flames burned within its hollow eye sockets.","Another Forgotten Guardian.","Damien immediately drew his sword.","\"Oh. Another one.\"","He grinned confidently.","\"Let’s kill it quickly. We can continue this conversation afterward.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Agreed.\"","However just as they prepared to charge. Another heavy footstep echoed through the corridor.","THUD!","A second Forgotten Guardian stepped out from the darkness behind the first.","THUD!","A third.","A moment later.","THUD!","A fourth.","The narrow corridor suddenly became filled with towering stone guardians.","Four Forgotten Guardians stood before them.","Silence.","Neither Noah nor Damien spoke for several seconds.","They simply stared at the overwhelming sight.","Finally Noah slowly exhaled.","\"...Fuck.\""]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: Labyrinth [5]","paragraphs":["After somehow managing to defeat the four stone guardians without suffering any major injuries, Noah and Damien continued deeper into the labyrinth.","Damien had taken care of two of the guardians with his overwhelming physical strength, while Noah had dealt with the remaining two by combining his swordsmanship with his Ice Creation ability. Although the battle had not been particularly difficult, it had drained a noticeable amount of their stamina and mana.","Still, neither of them slowed down.","The ancient corridors stretched endlessly before them.","Time and again, they reached intersections where several passageways branched off in different directions. Each time, Damien relied solely on his intuition to choose a route, while Noah silently followed behind.","More than once, they encountered hidden traps concealed beneath the stone floor or within the walls, but thanks to their growing caution, they managed to avoid most of them before any real danger arose.","The labyrinth never remained quiet for long.","Every now and then, another stone guardian would emerge from the darkness, forcing the two young men into battle once again.","Hours passed like that.","All they did was fight and walk then choose another path.","Repeat.","Eventually, even Noah began to lose track of how many corridors they had crossed.","Finally, both Noah and Damien collapsed onto the cold stone floor inside another unfamiliar passage.","Neither of them had the slightest idea where they were anymore.","\"This place...\" Damien muttered between heavy breaths. \"...It’s like an endless maze.\"","Noah leaned against the wall and let out a tired sigh.","\"You’re only realizing that now?\"","Damien chuckled weakly.","\"How many hours have we been wandering around?\"","Noah looked up at the stone ceiling.","\"Six... maybe seven.\"","He paused for a moment before shaking his head.","\"...Or perhaps even longer. I didn’t bother checking the time when we entered.\"","Damien groaned dramatically.","\"Seriously... how did Master Morgana explore this entire labyrinth and come back within a single day?\"","Noah folded his arms.","\"She probably used some mysterious witchcraft that pointed her toward the correct path.\"","Damien immediately rolled his eyes.","\"Master doesn’t know any magic like that.\"","He looked at Noah with complete seriousness.","\"Stop talking nonsense.\"","Noah merely shrugged.","\"I was just making a guess.\"","Silence settled between them once again.","After a few moments, Noah spoke.","\"Should we take a proper break?\"","He stretched his sore shoulders before continuing,","\"Your master did mention that clearing this labyrinth might take us several days. I hope you brought enough food and supplies.\"","Damien puffed out his chest proudly.","\"Of course I did.\"","He tapped the storage ring on his finger.","\"I came fully prepared.\"","\"Good.\"","Noah nodded with satisfaction.","At least they would not starve inside this endless stone prison.","The two of them took out several preserved meals, bread, dried meat, and bottles of water from their storage rings before quietly eating together.","For the first time since entering the labyrinth, neither of them spoke much.","The silence was strangely comforting.","After finishing his meal, Noah stood up and pulled a travel bag from his storage ring.","He placed it on the ground before lying down, using it as a pillow.","Damien remained seated with his back against the stone wall, his sword resting across his knees as he kept watch over the corridor.","Someone had to stay alert.","The labyrinth was far too dangerous for both of them to sleep at the same time.","As Noah closed his eyes, Damien suddenly broke the silence.","\"By the way... Noah.\"","\"Hm?\"","Without opening his eyes, Noah answered lazily.","\"Did you ever know anything about Mary’s family?\"","Noah remained quiet for a brief moment before replying.","\"No.\"","He slowly shook his head.","\"Apparently, she was an orphan.\"","A faint, complicated smile appeared on his face.","\"To be honest... even I didn’t know that while she was alive.\"","He spoke quietly.","\"I never asked about her family... and she never brought it up either.\"","His voice gradually became softer.","\"So... I never had the chance to know.\"","Damien lowered his gaze.","\"So... there really wasn’t anyone waiting for her.\"","Noah didn’t answer.","He simply kept his eyes closed.","The corridor became silent once again.","Only the faint crackling of the mana torches echoed through the ancient labyrinth as the two friends rested before continuing their uncertain journey deeper into the endless maze.","---","\"We did it?\"","Damien looked around the enormous chamber, his voice carrying both relief and disbelief.","\"It... seems so.\"","Noah slowly scanned the surroundings.","\"This is the first place we’ve seen that’s different from all the endless corridors.\"","It felt like they had spend one whole day or maybe more time to find this place.","The chamber was far larger than any they had encountered before.","Ancient stone pillars lined both sides, supporting the high ceiling overhead. At the very end of the chamber stood a colossal stone door covered with intricate carvings. Unlike the other doors they had passed, this one possessed an ancient, imposing aura.","Damien pointed toward it.","\"That door...It probably leads to the next floor.\"","Noah nodded.","\"That’s what it looks like. we might go more underground.\"","A faint smile appeared on both of their faces.","Perhaps they had finally found a way forward.","Just as they prepared to move.","Screech!!","A sharp, ear-piercing cry echoed above them.","\"What?\"","Both young men instinctively looked upward.","Something enormous dropped from the ceiling.","BOOM!","Two gigantic spiders landed heavily on the stone floor.","Their bodies were covered in thick black chitin, each standing nearly three meters tall. Eight crimson eyes glowed ominously in the dim chamber, while massive fangs continuously dripped with dark green venom that hissed whenever it touched the ground.","Unlike the stone guardians, these were living monsters. They possess flesh and blood.","Creatures of flesh and blood. The spiders let out another terrifying screech before charging.","Damien grinned.","\"One each?\"","Noah calmly drew his sword.","\"Sounds good.\"","Without another word both of them dashed forward.","Damien rushed toward the spider on the left.","Noah chose the one on the right."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Labyrinth [6]","paragraphs":["The monster immediately opened its enormous jaws.","Screech!!","Its grotesque mouth expanded unnaturally before spitting a massive stream of sticky webbing directly toward Noah.","Whoosh!","The web shot through the air at frightening speed.","Noah’s expression remained completely calm.","Slash!","His sword flashed once.","The mana-coated blade sliced cleanly through the incoming web before it could reach him.","The sticky strands fell harmlessly onto the stone floor.","The spider barely had time to react.","With nothing more than a single thought, more than thirty ice weapons materialized above the battlefield.","Swords.","Spears.","Daggers.","Lances.","Every weapon shimmered with an icy blue glow as they floated silently in the air.","The giant spider instinctively looked upward.","Its crimson eyes widened.","Noah calmly raised his free hand.","’Go.’","The instant the command left his lips every ice weapon shot downward simultaneously.","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","Whoosh!","The chamber filled with piercing whistles. The barrage descended like a rain of frozen death.","The spider tried to leap away but it was already too late.","Schhk!","Schhk!","Schhk!","One weapon after another pierced through its hard exoskeleton.","The creature let out a painful screech as countless blades tore through its flesh, pinning its enormous body to the stone floor.","Dark green blood splattered across the chamber. The monster struggled violently.","Its legs thrashed wildly. But the weapons had already locked it in place.","Noah slowly raised his left hand.","Then he calmly clenched his fist.","Crack!","Every ice weapon embedded inside the spider exploded at once. Jagged ice crystals burst outward from each blade, rapidly spreading through the monster’s body.","The frost raced across its flesh.","Its legs froze solid. Its movements slowed.","Within only a few seconds, the gigantic spider had become a motionless sculpture covered in thick layers of crystal-blue ice on many parts of body where those ice weapons clashed.","Noah walked forward without hesitation. His footsteps echoed softly through the chamber.","The frozen monster could no longer resist.","He raised his sword. Then brought it down in one clean motion.","Slash!","The blade severed the spider’s head effortlessly.","Its massive body trembled once before collapsing completely.","Dead.","Noah calmly shook the blood from his sword before looking toward Damien.","On the opposite side of the chamber...","Damien had already finished his own battle.","Golden mana still flickered around his body as the corpse of the second giant spider crashed onto the stone floor.","He rested his sword on his shoulder and smiled.","\"Looks like we’re done.\"","Noah returned his sword to his side.","\"That was easier than the golems.\"","Damien nodded in agreement.","\"Living monsters are much simpler. They don’t hit nearly as hard.\"","The two exchanged a satisfied glance before turning their attention toward the enormous stone door waiting silently at the end of the chamber.","Both walked toward it and stopped.","Damien stepped toward the enormous stone door and placed both hands against it, preparing to push it open.","\"Let’s see what’s on the next floor.\"","Just as he was about to apply force.","\"Wait a minute, Damien.\"","Damien paused and looked over his shoulder.","\"What?\"","Noah walked closer, his blue eyes fixed on the massive door.","\"I mean... look at it properly.\"","Damien frowned before following Noah’s gaze. Only then did he truly observe the intricate carvings engraved across the ancient black metal.","His eyes slowly widened. The door itself was a masterpiece.","Countless elegant patterns intertwined across its surface, depicting mountains, clouds, and forgotten runes whose meanings had long been lost to history.","But what drew both of their attention the most was the colossal dragon carved into its center.","The dragon covered nearly the entire door.","Since the door itself was forged from black metal, the dragon possessed the same obsidian appearance. Yet somehow, it stood out from everything around it.","Its scales had been carved with unbelievable precision.","Every single scale looked razor-sharp, layered perfectly upon the next, as though they would move if the creature suddenly came to life.","Its enormous wings spread majestically across both halves of the door.","Its powerful neck stretched upward while its jaws remained wide open in a silent roar that somehow still carried an overwhelming sense of dominance.","The craftsmanship was so lifelike that it almost felt alive.","The most striking feature, however was its eyes. Two crimson gemstones had been embedded into the dragon’s eye sockets.","Even after countless years, they still gleamed faintly in the torchlight.","Noah stepped closer.","Without saying a word, he reached out and rubbed one of the crimson gems with his thumb before trying to pry it loose.","It refused to move. Not even slightly.","Damien watched with amusement.","\"...It’s really beautiful.\"","He continued staring at the magnificent carving.","\"And overwhelming.\"","Noah nodded in agreement while withdrawing his hand.","\"Yeah.\"","His gaze remained fixed on the dragon.","\"But... Why a dragon?\"","Damien folded his arms. \"Maybe the one who built this labyrinth was a dragon.\"","Noah slowly turned his head toward him. His expression became completely deadpan.","Damien scratched the back of his head.","\"...What?\"","Noah sighed.","\"Damien... If a dragon—or any other mythical creature of that caliber—had created this labyrinth...\"","He looked back at the gigantic carving.","\"...do you honestly think two weak academy students like us could clear it?\"","Damien blinked.","\"...Hmm.\"","After thinking about it for a moment, he nodded.","\"That’s true.\"","Dragons weren’t ordinary magical beasts. They were mythical beings that existed only in ancient legends and the oldest historical records.","It was said that every true dragon possessed the potential to naturally reach the Mythical Rank.","As far as Noah knew, no human in recorded history had ever possessed Mythical Core potential except for the legendary Hero stories, and Damien himself. Also Noah included.","Yet even that wasn’t what made dragons truly terrifying.","According to the myths, dragons weren’t limited to the Mythical Rank.","They possessed the ability to surpass it and step into an even higher realm—a level so mysterious that no human, elf, beastman, or demon truly understood what lay beyond.","Whether those legends were true. Noah had no idea.","Still, one thing was certain. If a genuine dragon had truly created this labyrinth it would have been impossible for people at their level to survive inside it.","Damien chuckled awkwardly.","\"I guess I didn’t think that far.\"","\"You rarely do.\"","\"Tch.\"","Noah smiled faintly before placing both hands against the enormous door.","\"Anyway... Let’s head to the next floor.\"","Damien nodded and stepped beside him.","\"Right.\"","The two of them pushed together. The ancient door trembled before slowly beginning to open.","A deep metallic groan echoed throughout the chamber.","Rumble...","As the gap widened, cold air drifted out from the darkness beyond.","Noah stared into the pitch-black passage waiting on the other side.","’I wonder... Do dragons still exist somewhere in this world? After all... they’ve become nothing more than gods’ legends and ancient fairy tales.’","---","After walking down to stairs they came to underground floor.","\"Now... what are they?\" Damien asked.","Noah sighed and replied.","\"Mirrors.\""]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: Labyrinth [7]","paragraphs":["Before descending to the next floor, Noah and Damien followed a short flight of ancient stone stairs.","Their footsteps echoed softly through the silent passage.","Soon, they reached a small chamber. Unlike the massive halls they had explored earlier, this room was almost empty.","Only one object rested at its center. A treasure chest.","Both of their eyes lit up instantly.","\"A treasure chest!\"","Damien rubbed his hands together excitedly.","\"Finally! This has to be something good.\"","Noah nodded.","\"I hope so.\"","Treasure chests inside labyrinths usually contained valuable rewards. Ancient artifacts, rare weapons, powerful monster cores, or even forgotten inheritances.","At least that was how it usually happened in stories.","Damien cautiously walked toward the chest. He examined it carefully for a few seconds before slowly lifting the lid.","Creak.","The old hinges groaned loudly.","Both young men immediately leaned forward.","\"...\"","\"...\"","The excitement on their faces gradually disappeared.","Inside the chest lay only a handful of monster cores and several neatly bundled medicinal herbs.","There was nothing else.","Damien scratched the back of his head awkwardly.","\"Well... I guess they’re still useful.\"","Noah sighed helplessly.","\"They are...Just not what I was expecting.\"","His gaze unconsciously shifted toward Damien.","’Seriously...Isn’t this guy supposed to be the protagonist?’","Shouldn’t people like him discover legendary weapons, mysterious inheritances, or ancient treasures hidden inside places like this?","Instead they had found ordinary monster cores and medicinal herbs.","It wasn’t as though they were worthless.","Monster cores sold for decent prices, while the herbs could be used by alchemists to create valuable potions.","Still they were painfully ordinary.","Maybe I’m expecting too much. This labyrinth isn’t particularly high-ranked.","Shaking away the unnecessary thoughts, Noah stored everything inside his storage ring.","\"Let’s keep moving.\"","\"Yeah.\"","Leaving the chamber behind, the two stepped through another ancient stone doorway.","The instant they crossed the threshold...","Both of them stopped.","\"...\"","\"...\"","A massive hall stretched endlessly before them.","Neither of them could see where it ended.","The entire chamber was filled with gigantic mirrors.","Hundreds or perhaps thousands. Some reached all the way to the ceiling.","Others stood like enormous walls, creating countless intersections and narrow pathways.","Every direction they looked...","There were mirrors.","The place immediately reminded Noah of the mirror mazes from amusement parks back on Earth.","High above, dozens of mana lamps floated near the ceiling.","Their pale blue light illuminated the chamber just enough to reveal the countless reflections surrounding them.","The dim glow created an eerie atmosphere.","Shadows danced endlessly across the polished glass.","Damien slowly turned in a circle.","\"I guess... it’s another maze. But with mirrors.\"","Noah nodded.","\"Yeah. And I really hope it doesn’t take us another entire day to get through this one.\"","Damien smirked confidently.","\"It won’t.\"","\"I hope you’re right.\"","\"Come on.\"","The two cautiously stepped inside. As they walked deeper. Noah looked around in amazement.","\"Wow... Look. We’re everywhere.\"","Every mirror reflected them from different angles.","Some showed their fronts. Others showed their sides.","Many reflected other mirrors, creating endless copies of both Noah and Damien.","It looked as though hundreds of them were wandering through the labyrinth together.","Damien chuckled. \"Haha, this reminded me of mirror house in amusement parks or circus.\"","\"Yeah. Just don’t get confused by all these reflections.\"","Before Noah could finish,","Thud!","\"Ouch!\"","Noah walked straight into what he thought was an open passage.","Instead his face slammed directly against solid glass.","He immediately covered his nose with both hands.","\"Dammit... That hurt.\"","Damien burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! Noah, at least watch where you’re going. You literally walked into a mirror. I mean come on a mirror was in front so naturally you could see reflection in front. Why did you still walk.\"","Noah glared at him.","\"Very funny.\"","Damien grinned proudly before turning around.","Thud!","\"Ow!\"","This time he walked directly into another mirror himself.","Noah silently stared at him.","\"...\"","\"...\"","They looked at one another for several seconds.","Then both sighed simultaneously.","\"Let’s pretend neither of us saw that.\"","\"Agreed.\"","They resumed walking.","Then Noah suddenly stopped.","\"...Damien.\"","\"What?\"","\"Look carefully.\"","Damien frowned.","Both of them stared at the mirror Noah had just pointed toward. It was the mirror where Noah just collided.","His eyes slowly narrowed.","\"There... There isn’t any reflection.\"","That’s why he was walked into it.","Damien blinked.","Sure enough the mirror directly in front of them reflected absolutely nothing.","It looked like an ordinary sheet of polished glass.","Meanwhile, the mirrors behind them still displayed their figures.","Something about those reflections felt...","There was something very wrong about them.","Noah’s breathing slowed. The reflections behind them weren’t showing their backs.","Instead every single reflection faced them directly.","There were each Noah and each Damien.","They all stood inside the mirrors...","They were eatching them.","And then one by one they smiled.","A cold chill slowly crawled down Noah’s spine.","His heartbeat accelerated.","Without thinking he immediately turned around.","\"...\"","The mirrors showed perfectly normal reflections.","Since he was now looking at them. His front reflected. While Damien’s back, since he was not turned around like Noah.","He didn’t saw anthing unusual.","No smiling figures. No strange expressions. Everything appeared completely ordinary.","Noah frowned.","’Weird for a moment...I really felt like someone was watching us.’","He rubbed the back of his neck.","\"...Must’ve been my imagination. Let’s get out of here as quickly as possible.\"","Noah said worriedly.","\"This place gives me a bad feeling.\"","Damien nodded seriously.","\"Honestly... I’ve felt uncomfortable ever since we entered. The echoes...The reflections...Everything about this place feels wrong.\"","Neither of them joked anymore.","They carefully continued deeper into the maze.","Thud.","\"...Again.\"","Noah had walked into another invisible mirror.","\"...Who designed this stupid place?\"","Several minutes later.","Thud!","Damien collided with yet another mirror.","\"Tch. This is getting annoying.\"","They slowly advanced while constantly checking each step.","Even then the countless reflections made it almost impossible to distinguish real paths from dead ends.","Noah rubbed his forehead in frustration.","\"Dammit... This place is ridiculous.\"","He turned toward Damien, who stood only a few steps away.","\"Damien.\"","Without thinking Noah walked toward him.","Thud!","His forehead slammed into another mirror.","\"Ow!\"","He stumbled backward. Then his expression froze.","\"...Wait.\"","His eyes widened.","If I hit a mirror...","’Then was that...Damien’s reflection? Then where is he if not beside me?’","He immediately looked around. Countless Damiens stood throughout the maze.","Each one looked completely real. Each one copied every movement perfectly.","Noah couldn’t tell which one was the real Damien anymore.","Just then—","\"NOAH!\"","The shout echoed throughout the gigantic chamber.","Noah flinched.","The voice bounced endlessly between the mirrors.","It was impossible to determine where it had come from.","\"You come here!\" Noah shouted back.","His own voice echoed just as loudly.","Moments later, one of the Damiens began running toward him.","But after only a few steps.","Thud!","He crashed face-first into another mirror.","\"Dammit!\"","Damien cursed loudly. Enough was enough.","He drew his sword. Golden mana erupted around the blade. He decided to destroy this all mirrors. That was the best option he could think of.","With a powerful swing.","Slash!","A crescent-shaped arc of golden energy shot forward.","BOOM!!","The mirror in front of him exploded. Glass fragments scattered everywhere.","Dust and smoke filled the corridor. For a brief moment.","Neither Noah nor Damien could see anything.","Then the dust slowly settled.","Damien’s pupils shrank. Standing where the shattered mirror had been was another Damien.","He looked exactly the same. The same face. The same clothes.","The same sword. Only his skin was unnaturally pale.","His eyes were completely black. And an unsettling smile stretched across his face.","A cold shiver ran through Damien’s entire body.","The smiling doppelgänger tilted its head.","Then it lunged at him.","Everything instantly descended into chaos.","From Noah’s position, countless mirrors reflected the battle from every direction and in different angles.","Everywhere he looked there were dozens of Damiens.","Dozens of black-eyed doppelgängers.","Dozens of flashing swords. The reflections overlapped endlessly.","He couldn’t tell... Which Damien was the real one. And which one had come out of the mirror.","’I need to do something.’","Noah immediately drew his sword.","Mana surged from his core and flowed into his arm.","Without hesitation, he placed his free hand against the nearest mirror.","A thin layer of crystalline ice rapidly spread across its smooth surface.","Crack...","Crack...","The frost continued expanding as Noah moved alongside the mirror, freezing every inch he touched.","He kept advancing while coating the mirrors in ice, slowly making his way toward Damien and his doppelgänger.","His eyes remained fixed on the battle ahead.","BOOM!!","Another mirror shattered under the force of Damien’s sword.","\"Shit!\"","Damien’s expression changed instantly.","From the broken mirror another Damien stepped out.","It had the same appearance. The same light armor. The same weapon.","The only difference was its deathly pale skin and completely black eyes. And the copy couldn’t use light element that Damien used.","A sinister smile spread across its face.","Noah’s heart sank.","\"Damien! Stop destroying the mirrors!\"","Without wasting another second, Noah increased his speed and rushed toward him, continuing to freeze every mirror along his path before any more doppelgängers could emerge."]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: Labyrinth [8]","paragraphs":["The newly created doppelgänger wasted no time.","The moment it emerged from the shattered mirror, it kicked off the ground and charged straight toward Damien.","Its speed was astonishing.","There swordsmanship looked similar to Damien.","\"Dammit!\"","Damien immediately raised his sword to block.","Clang!!","The two identical blades collided violently. A shockwave swept through the chamber.","For a brief moment, even Damien couldn’t tell whether he was fighting a copy or himself.","The doppelgänger pressed forward relentlessly, forcing Damien backward with a flurry of powerful strikes.","Clang!","Clang!","Clang!","Each collision echoed throughout the mirror hall.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","’I can’t let another one join the fight.’","Mana surged through his body.","He thrust his left hand toward the charging doppelgänger. He could only hope that it’s not another reflection.","Ice Creation kicked in.","The stone floor beneath the creature suddenly trembled.","Crack!","Jagged pillars of ice burst upward from below. The doppelgänger sensed the danger and attempted to leap away.","But it was too late.","More spikes erupted from every direction.","Within a heartbeat, enormous pillars of crystal-blue ice surrounded it, trapping its body inside a frozen cage.","The doppelgänger struggled violently.","’Yes!’ Noah thought.","Cracks spread across the ice as it attempted to break free.","Noah didn’t give it the opportunity. With another thought a long spear forged entirely from compressed ice materialized behind him.","Cold mist flowed around its razor-sharp tip. Noah grabbed it without hesitation. His feet dug into the stone floor.","Then he threw it with every ounce of strength he possessed.","Whoosh!","The spear tore through the air like a bolt of frozen lightning.","The trapped doppelgänger barely managed to turn its head.","Schhk!","The icy spear pierced cleanly through its neck. The force carried it backward, pinning the creature against the frozen prison.","At the exact same moment Damien seized the opening.","Golden mana erupted around his blade.","He dashed forward.","Slash!","A brilliant arc of light flashed across the chamber. The sword sliced straight through the doppelgänger’s chest.","The copy froze for an instant. Then its body began cracking apart.","Black fractures spread across its pale skin before it shattered into countless fragments of black crystal that dissolved into smoke.","Silence returned.","Damien lowered his sword and let out a slow breath.","\"...Finally. This time I actually hit the enemy.\"","He glanced around the chamber.","\"...Instead of another mirror.\"","Noah couldn’t help smiling.","\"I was starting to think you’d destroy this entire floor before killing a single monster.\"","\"Tch.\"","Damien sheathed his sword.","\"That wasn’t my fault.\"","Noah walked over to him.","\"Damien. Stay exactly where you are. I’ll come to you.\"","Damien simply nodded.","\"Got it.\"","Noah carefully advanced through the maze. Instead of rushing, he moved slowly while placing one hand against the mirrors beside him.","Crystalline frost spread wherever his fingers touched.","A continuous trail of ice marked every path he had already crossed.","It wasn’t a perfect solution... But at least it prevented them from wandering in circles.","Several minutes later, Noah finally reached Damien.","He exhaled quietly.","\"Let’s move slowly. And this time... Let’s be much more careful.\"","Damien nodded seriously.","\"Yeah. I don’t want any more copies of myself.\"","The two resumed their journey. Every step echoed endlessly through the labyrinth.","The deeper they walked. The stranger the mirrors became.","Sometimes their reflections behaved normally. Other times the reflections seemed just a fraction of a second slower.","As though something inside the mirrors was observing them rather than merely reflecting them.","A chill ran down Noah’s spine.","\"...Noah.\"","Damien called his name.","Noah instinctively turned toward the voice on his left.","The Damien standing inside the mirror smiled warmly at him.","\"Noah.\"","\"Over here.\"","His voice sounded perfectly natural.","Before Noah could react—","The real Damien spoke from his right.","\"I’m on your right. Don’t listen to them.\"","Noah immediately turned.","There stood the real Damien.","He sighed in relief.","\"I know. They’re copying our voices now.\"","Damien frowned.","\"This place keeps getting creepier. The lighting doesn’t help either.\"","The pale blue glow from the mana lamps made every reflection appear ghostly.","Noah nodded.","\"It honestly feels like we’re trapped inside a haunted house.\"","\"Hehehe~ Noah~\"","A soft laugh echoed through the mirrors.","\"Hehehe~ Damien~\"","Both young men froze.","Dozens of reflections were smiling. Each one called their names in an eerily sweet voice.","Noah shuddered.","\"...Hearing your voice call my name like that...in such sweet tone...is unbelievably creepy and disgusting.\"","Damien grimaced.","\"I know that. Even I hate hearing myself sound like that.\"","The two exchanged an uneasy look before continuing deeper into the endless maze.","---","While Noah and Damien struggled through the mysterious labyrinth...","Far away from them, in an unknown corner of the empire...","Cold winds swept through a vast emerald forest.","Towering ancient trees rose toward the sky, their thick canopies blocking out most of the moonlight. Only a few pale rays filtered through the countless leaves, casting shifting patterns across the forest floor.","The woodland was unnaturally quiet.","Only the occasional rustling of leaves and the distant cries of birds disturbed the silence.","A lone figure sprinted through the dense forest at astonishing speed.","Branches whipped past him as his boots barely touched the ground before launching him forward again.","Despite maintaining such a relentless pace, his breathing remained perfectly steady.","The man appeared to be in his early forties.","He possessed short brown hair, sharp black eyes, and a rugged face that bore the marks of countless battles.","It was none other than...","Cassian Nightfall. Uncle of Kaelan Nightfall.","He continued running deeper into the forest. After several more minutes.","His pace suddenly slowed. Then he came to an abrupt stop.","His sharp eyes narrowed as he look at the place in front of him.","\"...Did someone come here before me?\"","His gaze settled upon an ancient structure hidden among the trees.","Standing before him was a weathered shrine. Time had left countless scars upon it.","The wooden pillars had faded with age, while patches of moss and creeping vines had claimed much of its exterior.","Despite its condition, the architecture remained magnificent.","Its sweeping roofs, elegant wooden beams, and towering entrance gate resembled the ancient shrines once found in old Japanese architecture.","It looked as though the place had stood there for centuries...","Forgotten by civilization.","Cassian silently approached.","The enormous shrine gate stood wide open.","Someone had entered recently.","Why he came to that conclusion? because he could see the building even from afar.","His expression grew colder. Without hesitation, he walked through the gate and headed toward the main building.","The front entrance had been left open.","He stepped inside."]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: Dragon Of Storm And Lightning","paragraphs":["Creak...","Creak...","The aged wooden floor groaned beneath his footsteps. His gaze slowly swept across the abandoned shrine.","Dust covered nearly every surface. Spider webs stretched between the pillars.","The faint scent of damp wood lingered in the air.","Everything suggested the shrine had long since been abandoned.","There was no offering table.","There was no incense. there was no worshippers.","No signs that anyone had prayed here for generations.","At first glance it appeared to be nothing more than a forgotten ruin.","Cassian continued walking until he reached the main hall.","His eyes finally settled upon the object standing at its center.","There was no statue of a god.","Instead...","Mounted within an enormous metal frame was a magnificent relief carved directly into black steel.","A dragon. the being worship by people in past.","Its scales shimmered with an intricate dark-blue pattern despite the passage of countless years. Its enormous wings spread proudly behind it.","Its jaws were opened in a silent roar toward the heavens.","Even carved from lifeless metal. The dragon radiated overwhelming majesty.","Cassian gazed at it silently.","\"...The Dragon of Lightning and Storm.\"","His voice echoed softly through the empty shrine.","For several moments...","He simply stood there.","Then he lowered his gaze toward the old wooden offering counter before the dragon. Ordinary visitors would have assumed it served only as a place for offerings.","Cassian knew better.","He placed both hands against the heavy wooden structure.","Then he slowly pushed it aside.","Rumble...","The entire counter slid effortlessly across the floor.","Hidden beneath it. A narrow stone staircase descended into darkness.","Without hesitation Cassian stepped inside.","The stairs spiraled deep underground. The deeper he descended, the colder the air became.","Several minutes later he arrived before a plain stone wall.","There was nothing unusual about it.","There was no carvings. There was no doorway.","There was nothing.","Cassian calmly placed his right palm against the stone. Then he began chanting several unfamiliar words in an ancient language.","Mana flowed steadily from his body into the wall.","Moments later a massive magic circle slowly spread beneath his hand.","Ancient runes illuminated one after another.","The entire wall trembled.","Then it vanished. In its place appeared a heavy metal door covered with intricate symbols.","Cassian pushed it open.","Beyond it lay a small underground chamber. Unlike the abandoned shrine above...","This room had been carefully preserved.","Shelves lined every wall.","Dozens of ancient scrolls rested neatly upon them. Several wooden boxes sat undisturbed beneath thick layers of dust.","Cassian slowly exhaled.","\"...It’s been years since I last visited this place. I don’t even remember exactly how everything was arranged.\"","He walked directly toward one particular shelf. His destination was obvious.","A small wooden box rested there. He picked it up carefully.","Then opened it. Then there was silence for a moment. His eyes remained fixed on the empty interior.","It was as if the thing that was supposed to be inside was gone.","His expression darkened instantly.","An icy killing intent spread throughout the room.","\"...Someone took it. They took the scroll.\"","His voice became frighteningly calm. Then his brows slowly knitted together.","\"Damn it... I never thought that scroll would become important.\"","His fingers tightened around the wooden box.","\"It was only after Malrick urgently requested it that I realized its value.\"","He slowly closed the lid.","\"...Who entered this place?\"","His mind raced rapidly.","’Only Malrick and I know how to open the hidden chamber. No one else should even know this shrine exists. Then... Who did this?","For the first time in many years. Cassian felt genuinely disturbed.","He immediately left the underground chamber. The moment he stepped outside...","The hidden metal door disappeared. The stone wall returned to normal as though nothing had ever existed there.","Without wasting another second Cassian rushed back through the abandoned shrine.","He leaped onto its weathered rooftop in a single bound. Standing atop the ancient building...","He slowly closed his eyes.","Then—","Boom!","An overwhelming wave of mana erupted from his body. Invisible pressure spread across the surrounding forest in every direction.","Trees bent violently beneath the force. Birds scattered into the sky.","Small beasts fled in panic.","Cassian extended his senses as far as possible.","He searched every corner of the forest.","Every living presence. Every lingering trace of mana. He hoped whoever had stolen the scroll had only recently escaped.","But after several long moments. He found nothing.","Not a single clue. His eyes slowly opened.","Cold fury burned within them.","\"...Fuck.\"","The curse echoed across the silent forest.","---","Two cloaked figures finally emerged from the dense forest.","The moment they stepped onto the old dirt road, both of them bent forward, breathing heavily.","\"Haah...\"","\"Haah...\"","Their cloaks were covered in dust, and small scratches marked their clothes from forcing their way through the thick undergrowth.","Their faces were hidden by the hood.","\"Damn... We actually did it.\"","A relieved grin spread across his face under the hood.","\"We managed to get out without getting caught.\"","The second man let out an exhausted sigh.","\"Fuck... I’m never coming with you again.\"","\"You dragged me into the middle of some suspicious abandoned shrine in the middle of nowhere.\"","The first man laughed.","\"I didn’t have a choice.\"","\"You’re the best person I know when it comes to locating hidden chambers and breaking ancient seals.\"","The second man rolled his eyes.","\"Yeah, yeah...\"","\"Keep flattering me.\"","He stretched his aching shoulders before glaring at his companion.","\"But seriously...\"","\"Where did you even learn about that place? That hidden mechanism wasn’t something ordinary.\"","He shook his head in disbelief.","\"It took us nearly an entire day just to analyze those ancient runes and dismantle the protective formation. If even a single sequence had been wrong...that place would’ve probably buried us alive.\"","The first man simply shrugged.","\"But we succeeded. That’s all that matters.\"","The second man folded his arms.","\"Fine. We got what we came for.\"","He looked toward his companion with narrowed eyes.","\"So... Care to explain what exactly is inside that scroll?\"","The cloaked man smiled faintly. He reached into his storage ring.","A moment later, an ancient scroll appeared in his hand.","Its dark-blue bindings were covered with faded golden runes, while an unfamiliar dragon emblem had been engraved into the seal.","He slowly examined it.","\"What’s inside...\"","He chuckled softly.","\"I honestly have no idea.\"","The other man blinked.","\"You stole something without knowing what it was?\"","The cloaked man nodded casually.","\"Pretty much.\"","His fingers traced the dragon emblem on the scroll.","\"But... I have a feeling it’s related to the Dragon of Lightning and Storm. Or maybe... multiple dragons.\"","His companion stared at him for several seconds before rubbing his forehead.","\"...Sometimes I seriously wonder how you’re still alive.\"","The cloaked man merely smiled as he tucked the ancient scroll safely back into his storage ring.","\"I suppose... We’ll find out soon enough.\""]}]);
